-- Regulation W (12 CFR Part 223), slice B: an INDEPENDENT test file.
--
-- Written independently from the regulation text (the four source files: 223.3; 223.11 to 223.16;
-- 223.21 to 223.24; 223.41 and 223.42) and from the INTERFACE (types, signatures and @refs, with every
-- body answering FALSE, 0 or the first constructor), BEFORE the encoding was read.
-- Every expected value was decided from the words of the regulation and then left alone.
--
-- Target compiler: main (1.6.112).  Each #ASSERT is one line; a trailing comment says what the case exercises.
-- Where two readings of the words both fit, the assertions that depend on the choice are in the last section,
-- `Contested readings`, each naming its R-number in independent-readings-b.md.
-- Conventions that are about the interface rather than the regulation (percent scale, what a field holds) are
-- listed in independent-readings-b.md under "Interface assumptions".
-- Percent arguments are written as the regulation prints them: 10 means 10 percent, 130 means 130 percent.
--
-- Notation in the comments: a case marked "alone" changes exactly one input from the baseline above it.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `regw-nouns`
IMPORT `regw-control`
IMPORT `regw-affiliate`
IMPORT `regwb-nouns`
IMPORT `regwb-covered`
IMPORT `regwb-collateral`
IMPORT `regwb-lowquality`
IMPORT `regwb-valuation`
IMPORT `regwb-effects`
IMPORT `regwb-exemptions-41`
IMPORT `regwb-exemptions-42`
IMPORT `regwb-assessment`


§ `Fixtures: one member bank and the companies around it`

-- Acme Bank is the member bank.  Acme Holdings owns all of its common stock (a parent: an affiliate).
-- Acme Mortgage Co and Acme Sister Bank are owned by Acme Holdings (companies under common control: affiliates).
-- Acme Fin Sub is a financial subsidiary of the bank (an affiliate).  Stranger Corp has no tie to anyone.

GIVEN n IS A STRING, k IS A `Party kind`, di IS A BOOLEAN, fs IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Party
`a party` MEANS Party OF n, k, di, fs, `Some other activity`, `Not held through a debt previously contracted`, FALSE

GIVEN h IS A STRING, i IS A STRING
GIVETH A Holding
`a wholly owned holding` MEANS Holding OF h, i, "common", 100, 100, FALSE, FALSE

`the structure` MEANS Structure OF "Acme Bank", (LIST (`a party` "Acme Bank" Corporation TRUE FALSE), (`a party` "Acme Holdings" Corporation FALSE FALSE), (`a party` "Acme Mortgage Co" Corporation FALSE FALSE), (`a party` "Acme Fin Sub" Corporation FALSE TRUE), (`a party` "Acme Sister Bank" Corporation TRUE FALSE), (`a party` "Stranger Corp" Corporation FALSE FALSE)), (LIST (`a wholly owned holding` "Acme Holdings" "Acme Bank"), (`a wholly owned holding` "Acme Holdings" "Acme Mortgage Co"), (`a wholly owned holding` "Acme Bank" "Acme Fin Sub"), (`a wholly owned holding` "Acme Holdings" "Acme Sister Bank")), EMPTY, EMPTY, EMPTY, EMPTY, EMPTY, EMPTY, EMPTY

`the readings` MEANS Readings OF `The member bank is not its own affiliate`, `One board at a time: the member bank, or one controlling company`, `Control through the controller's own holdings and elections, without attribution`, `A subsidiary of a company described in paragraphs (a)(1) through (10) only`

-- The same readings but with the member bank its own affiliate on the literal words (223.2(a)(2) with 223.3(f)), used only in R11.
`the literal readings` MEANS Readings OF `The member bank is its own affiliate on the literal words`, `One board at a time: the member bank, or one controlling company`, `Control through the controller's own holdings and elections, without attribution`, `A subsidiary of a company described in paragraphs (a)(1) through (10) only`

-- Short names for the kinds of transaction (223.3(h)(1) to (5) and the netting arrangement) and of collateral.
GIVETH A `Transaction kind`
kCredit MEANS `An extension of credit`
GIVETH A `Transaction kind`
kSecurity MEANS `A purchase of, or an investment in, a security`
GIVETH A `Transaction kind`
kAsset MEANS `A purchase of an asset`
GIVETH A `Transaction kind`
kAccept MEANS `The acceptance of a security as collateral for an extension of credit`
GIVETH A `Transaction kind`
kGuarantee MEANS `The issuance of a guarantee, acceptance or letter of credit, or the confirmation of a letter of credit`
GIVETH A `Transaction kind`
kNetting MEANS `A cross-affiliate netting arrangement`
GIVETH A `Transaction kind`
kOther MEANS `Some other transaction`

GIVETH A `Collateral kind`
cUS MEANS `Obligations of the United States or its agencies`
GIVETH A `Collateral kind`
cGuar MEANS `Obligations fully guaranteed by the United States or its agencies as to principal and interest`
GIVETH A `Collateral kind`
cNotes MEANS `Notes, drafts, bills of exchange or bankers' acceptances eligible for rediscount or purchase by a Federal Reserve Bank`
GIVETH A `Collateral kind`
cDeposit MEANS `A segregated, earmarked deposit account with the member bank for the sole purpose of securing credit transactions with affiliates`
GIVETH A `Collateral kind`
cState MEANS `Obligations of a State or political subdivision of a State`
GIVETH A `Collateral kind`
cDebt MEANS `Other debt instruments, including loans and other receivables`
GIVETH A `Collateral kind`
cProp MEANS `Stock, leases, or other real or personal property`
GIVETH A `Collateral kind`
cLow MEANS `A low-quality asset`
GIVETH A `Collateral kind`
cAffSec MEANS `A security issued by an affiliate`
GIVETH A `Collateral kind`
cOwnEq MEANS `An equity security of the member bank, or a debt security of the member bank that represents regulatory capital`
GIVETH A `Collateral kind`
cIntang MEANS `An intangible asset (including a servicing asset)`
GIVETH A `Collateral kind`
cGuarLC MEANS `A guarantee, letter of credit or other similar instrument`

-- Collateral is built positionally: kind, market value, senior security interest, senior credit, approved by the Board, perfected and enforceable.
-- "clean" is a first-priority, perfected interest with no Board approval.
GIVEN k IS A `Collateral kind`, v IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Collateral
`clean collateral` MEANS Collateral OF k, v, 0, 0, FALSE, TRUE

GIVEN k IS A `Collateral kind`, v IS A NUMBER, ssi IS A NUMBER, sc IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Collateral
`encumbered collateral` MEANS Collateral OF k, v, ssi, sc, FALSE, TRUE

GIVEN k IS A `Collateral kind`, v IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Collateral
`unperfected collateral` MEANS Collateral OF k, v, 0, 0, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN k IS A `Collateral kind`, v IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Collateral
`board approved collateral` MEANS Collateral OF k, v, 0, 0, TRUE, TRUE

-- Collateral exceptions: an acceptance already fully secured; unused portion; no obligation to advance until collateral is provided; a debt security of an affiliate bought from a nonaffiliate in a bona fide secondary market.
`no exceptions` MEANS `Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE

-- Asset condition: classified or specially treated; nonaccrual; days past due; renegotiated; acquired in satisfaction of a debt and not yet reviewed.
`a sound asset` MEANS `Asset condition` OF FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE
`a nonaccrual asset` MEANS `Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE

-- A participation renewal that satisfies every limb of 223.15(b) by the board route, with the bank's share equal to its proportional share and notice on day 20.
`a valid renewal` MEANS `Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20
`no renewal` MEANS `Participation renewal` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0, 0, FALSE, 0

GIVETH A `Five percent reading`
pp MEANS `Five percentage points above the proportional share`
GIVETH A `Five percent reading`
rel MEANS `Five percent more than the proportional share`


§ `223.3(h) and (i): covered transactions and credit transactions`

-- 223.3(i): a credit transaction with an affiliate is (1) an extension of credit, (2) a guarantee, acceptance or letter of credit
-- (including an endorsement or standby letter of credit) or a confirmation of a letter of credit, and (3) a cross-affiliate netting arrangement.
-- 223.3(h): a covered transaction is (1) an extension of credit, (2) a purchase of or investment in a security, (3) a purchase of an asset
-- (except purchases of real and personal property the Board has specifically exempted), (4) the acceptance of an affiliate's security as
-- collateral for an extension of credit to any person or company, (5) a guarantee, acceptance or letter of credit, and a cross-affiliate netting arrangement.
-- The kinds, one by one.
#ASSERT `is a credit transaction kind` kCredit   -- credit transaction kind: (i)(1)
#ASSERT `is a credit transaction kind` kGuarantee   -- credit transaction kind: (i)(2)
#ASSERT `is a credit transaction kind` kNetting   -- credit transaction kind: (i)(3)
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a credit transaction kind` kSecurity))   -- not a credit transaction kind: a purchase of a security is not in (i)
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a credit transaction kind` kAsset))   -- not a credit transaction kind: a purchase of an asset is not in (i)
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a credit transaction kind` kAccept))   -- not a credit transaction kind: accepting a security as collateral is not in (i)
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a credit transaction kind` kOther))   -- not a credit transaction kind: some other transaction is not in (i)
#ASSERT `is a kind of covered transaction` kCredit   -- covered kind: (h)(1) an extension of credit
#ASSERT `is a kind of covered transaction` kSecurity   -- covered kind: (h)(2) a purchase of a security
#ASSERT `is a kind of covered transaction` kAsset   -- covered kind: (h)(3) a purchase of an asset
#ASSERT `is a kind of covered transaction` kAccept   -- covered kind: (h)(4) acceptance of a security as collateral
#ASSERT `is a kind of covered transaction` kGuarantee   -- covered kind: (h)(5) a guarantee, acceptance or letter of credit
#ASSERT `is a kind of covered transaction` kNetting   -- covered kind: (h)(5) a cross-affiliate netting arrangement
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a kind of covered transaction` kOther))   -- some other transaction is in none of (h)(1) to (5)
-- Whether this transaction is a covered transaction: the affiliate named in it must be an affiliate (here Acme Holdings, a parent).
-- Here `with` and `affiliate concerned` are the same company, so the cases do not depend on which of the two the encoding tests (R1 covers the cases where they differ).
-- Transaction OF kind, with, affiliate concerned, value, exempted by the Board as a purchase of property.
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE)   -- affiliate, (h)(1) an extension of credit
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kSecurity, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE)   -- affiliate, (h)(2) a purchase of a security
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE)   -- affiliate, (h)(3) a purchase of an asset
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAccept, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE)   -- affiliate, (h)(4) acceptance of a security as collateral
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kGuarantee, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE)   -- affiliate, (h)(5) a guarantee, acceptance or letter of credit
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kNetting, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE)   -- affiliate, (h)(5) a cross-affiliate netting arrangement
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Mortgage Co", "Acme Mortgage Co", 100, FALSE)   -- an extension of credit to a sister company is covered
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Fin Sub", "Acme Fin Sub", 100, FALSE)   -- an extension of credit to a financial subsidiary of the bank is covered
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Sister Bank", "Acme Sister Bank", 100, FALSE)   -- an extension of credit to a depository institution under common control (section 23A) is covered
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 0, FALSE)   -- covered does not depend on the amount: a transaction of value 0
-- The same kinds with a nonaffiliate: none is covered.
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 100, FALSE)))   -- nonaffiliate, (h)(1) an extension of credit
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kSecurity, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 100, FALSE)))   -- nonaffiliate, (h)(2) a purchase of a security
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 100, FALSE)))   -- nonaffiliate, (h)(3) a purchase of an asset
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAccept, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 100, FALSE)))   -- nonaffiliate, (h)(4) acceptance of a security as collateral
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kGuarantee, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 100, FALSE)))   -- nonaffiliate, (h)(5) a guarantee, acceptance or letter of credit
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kNetting, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 100, FALSE)))   -- nonaffiliate, (h)(5) a cross-affiliate netting arrangement
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Nobody Ltd", "Nobody Ltd", 100, FALSE)))   -- a name that is not in the structure at all is not an affiliate
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kOther, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE)))   -- some other transaction with an affiliate is in none of (h)(1) to (5)
-- 223.3(h)(3): purchases of real and personal property specifically exempted by the Board are not covered.
-- The exemption is only of (h)(3), so the flag changes nothing for the other kinds.
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, TRUE)))   -- (h)(3): purchase of an asset from an affiliate that the Board exempted: not covered
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE)   -- (h)(3): the same purchase, not exempted: covered
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, TRUE)   -- the Board exemption of (h)(3) does not reach an extension of credit
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kSecurity, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, TRUE)   -- the Board exemption of (h)(3) does not reach a purchase of a security
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kGuarantee, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, TRUE)   -- the Board exemption of (h)(3) does not reach a guarantee

§ `223.3(a): the aggregate amount of covered transactions`

-- The amount about to be engaged in, added to the current amount of all outstanding covered transactions.
#ASSERT `aggregate amount of covered transactions` 100 200 EQUALS 300   -- 223.3(a): 100 about to be engaged in plus 200 outstanding
#ASSERT `aggregate amount of covered transactions` 0 0 EQUALS 0   -- 223.3(a): 0 about to be engaged in plus 0 outstanding
#ASSERT `aggregate amount of covered transactions` 100 0 EQUALS 100   -- 223.3(a): 100 about to be engaged in plus 0 outstanding
#ASSERT `aggregate amount of covered transactions` 0 200 EQUALS 200   -- 223.3(a): 0 about to be engaged in plus 200 outstanding
#ASSERT `aggregate amount of covered transactions` 0.5 0.25 EQUALS 0.75   -- 223.3(a): 0.5 about to be engaged in plus 0.25 outstanding
#ASSERT `aggregate amount of covered transactions` 1000 1 EQUALS 1001   -- 223.3(a): 1000 about to be engaged in plus 1 outstanding
-- 223.11 and 223.12 say a transaction is barred when the aggregate amount "would exceed" a percent of capital stock and surplus:
-- exactly the percent is not an excess; a cent over is.
#ASSERT (NOT (`exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` 100 1000 10))   -- exactly 10 percent does not exceed it (aggregate 100, css 1000, percent 10)
#ASSERT `exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` 100.01 1000 10   -- a cent over 10 percent exceeds it (aggregate 100.01, css 1000, percent 10)
#ASSERT (NOT (`exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` 99.99 1000 10))   -- a cent under 10 percent (aggregate 99.99, css 1000, percent 10)
#ASSERT (NOT (`exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` 200 1000 20))   -- exactly 20 percent does not exceed it (aggregate 200, css 1000, percent 20)
#ASSERT `exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` 200.01 1000 20   -- a cent over 20 percent exceeds it (aggregate 200.01, css 1000, percent 20)
#ASSERT (NOT (`exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` 199.99 1000 20))   -- a cent under 20 percent (aggregate 199.99, css 1000, percent 20)
#ASSERT (NOT (`exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` 25 100 25))   -- exactly 25 percent (the ceiling of 223.41(d)(6)) does not exceed it (aggregate 25, css 100, percent 25)
#ASSERT `exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` 25.01 100 25   -- a cent over 25 percent (aggregate 25.01, css 100, percent 25)
#ASSERT (NOT (`exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` 50 100 50))   -- exactly 50 percent (aggregate 50, css 100, percent 50)
#ASSERT `exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` 50.01 100 50   -- a cent over 50 percent (aggregate 50.01, css 100, percent 50)
#ASSERT `exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` 1 0 10   -- any positive aggregate exceeds 10 percent of zero (aggregate 1, css 0, percent 10)
#ASSERT (NOT (`exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` 0 1000 10))   -- an aggregate of zero exceeds nothing (aggregate 0, css 1000, percent 10)
#ASSERT `exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` 1001 1000 100   -- over 100 percent of capital stock and surplus (aggregate 1001, css 1000, percent 100)
#ASSERT (NOT (`exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` 1000 1000 100))   -- exactly 100 percent (aggregate 1000, css 1000, percent 100)

§ `223.11: the single-affiliate limit`

-- names a financial subsidiary: Acme Fin Sub is one (and is a subsidiary of the bank); the others are not.
#ASSERT `names a financial subsidiary` `the structure` "Acme Fin Sub"   -- Acme Fin Sub is flagged a financial subsidiary
#ASSERT (NOT (`names a financial subsidiary` `the structure` "Acme Holdings"))   -- not a financial subsidiary: a parent
#ASSERT (NOT (`names a financial subsidiary` `the structure` "Acme Mortgage Co"))   -- not a financial subsidiary: a sister company
#ASSERT (NOT (`names a financial subsidiary` `the structure` "Acme Sister Bank"))   -- not a financial subsidiary: a sister bank
#ASSERT (NOT (`names a financial subsidiary` `the structure` "Stranger Corp"))   -- not a financial subsidiary: a stranger
#ASSERT (NOT (`names a financial subsidiary` `the structure` "Nobody Ltd"))   -- not a financial subsidiary: not in the structure
#ASSERT (NOT (`names a financial subsidiary` `the structure` "Acme Bank"))   -- not a financial subsidiary: the member bank itself
-- 223.11: a member bank may not engage in a covered transaction with an affiliate (other than a financial subsidiary of the member bank)
-- if the aggregate amount of its covered transactions with that affiliate would exceed 10 percent of its capital stock and surplus.
-- Arguments: structure, readings, transaction, outstanding covered transactions with this affiliate, capital stock and surplus.
-- Capital stock and surplus is 1000 unless stated.
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE) 0 1000))   -- 223.11: exactly 10 percent of css, no outstanding
#ASSERT `would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100.01, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.11: a cent over 10 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 99.99, FALSE) 0 1000))   -- 223.11: a cent under 10 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 60, FALSE) 40 1000))   -- 223.11: 60 about to be engaged in plus 40 outstanding is exactly 10 percent
#ASSERT `would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 60, FALSE) 40.01 1000   -- 223.11: 60 plus 40.01 is a cent over
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 0.01, FALSE) 99.99 1000))   -- 223.11: the smallest step up to exactly 10 percent
#ASSERT `would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 0.01, FALSE) 100 1000   -- 223.11: a bank already at the limit may not add even a cent
#ASSERT `would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 0.01, FALSE) 500 1000   -- 223.11: a bank already over the limit may not add anything
#ASSERT `would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 150, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.11: 15 percent
#ASSERT `would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 1000, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.11: 100 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 20, FALSE) 0 200))   -- 223.11: capital stock and surplus 200, exactly 10 percent
#ASSERT `would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 20.01, FALSE) 0 200   -- 223.11: capital stock and surplus 200, a cent over 10 percent
#ASSERT `would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kSecurity, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100.01, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.11 applies to every covered kind: (h)(2) a purchase of a security
#ASSERT `would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100.01, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.11 applies to every covered kind: (h)(3) a purchase of an asset
#ASSERT `would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAccept, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100.01, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.11 applies to every covered kind: (h)(4) acceptance of a security as collateral
#ASSERT `would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kGuarantee, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100.01, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.11 applies to every covered kind: (h)(5) a guarantee, acceptance or letter of credit
#ASSERT `would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kNetting, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100.01, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.11 applies to every covered kind: (h)(5) a cross-affiliate netting arrangement
#ASSERT `would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Mortgage Co", "Acme Mortgage Co", 100.01, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.11: a sister company
#ASSERT `would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Sister Bank", "Acme Sister Bank", 100.01, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.11: a sister bank (a depository institution affiliate)
-- The financial-subsidiary carve-out: 223.11 does not apply to a financial subsidiary of the member bank.
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Fin Sub", "Acme Fin Sub", 150, FALSE) 0 1000))   -- 223.11 carve-out: a financial subsidiary, 15 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Fin Sub", "Acme Fin Sub", 1000, FALSE) 0 1000))   -- 223.11 carve-out: a financial subsidiary, 100 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kSecurity, "Acme Fin Sub", "Acme Fin Sub", 150, FALSE) 500 1000))   -- 223.11 carve-out: a financial subsidiary, large outstanding
-- What is not a covered transaction is not barred: a nonaffiliate, some other transaction, a Board-exempted purchase of property.
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 5000, FALSE) 0 1000))   -- 223.11: a loan to a nonaffiliate is not a covered transaction
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kOther, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 5000, FALSE) 0 1000))   -- 223.11: some other transaction with an affiliate is not covered
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 5000, TRUE) 0 1000))   -- 223.11: a Board-exempted purchase of property is not covered
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 5000, FALSE) 5000 1000))   -- 223.11: a nonaffiliate transaction is not barred even when the bank is over the limit elsewhere

§ `223.12: the all-affiliates limit`

-- 223.12: a member bank may not engage in a covered transaction with any affiliate if the aggregate amount of its covered transactions
-- with ALL affiliates would exceed 20 percent of capital stock and surplus.  It has no financial-subsidiary carve-out.
-- Arguments: structure, readings, transaction, outstanding with all affiliates, capital stock and surplus.
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 200, FALSE) 0 1000))   -- 223.12: exactly 20 percent of css
#ASSERT `would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 200.01, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.12: a cent over 20 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 199.99, FALSE) 0 1000))   -- 223.12: a cent under 20 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 60, FALSE) 140 1000))   -- 223.12: 60 plus 140 outstanding with all affiliates is exactly 20 percent
#ASSERT `would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 60, FALSE) 140.01 1000   -- 223.12: 60 plus 140.01 is a cent over
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 0.01, FALSE) 199.99 1000))   -- 223.12: the smallest step up to exactly 20 percent
#ASSERT `would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 0.01, FALSE) 200 1000   -- 223.12: at the limit, even a cent more is barred
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 150, FALSE) 0 1000))   -- 223.12: 15 percent is within the all-affiliates limit (it is the single limit that bites)
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE) 100 1000))   -- 223.12: 100 plus 100 is exactly 20 percent
#ASSERT `would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100.01, FALSE) 100 1000   -- 223.12: 100.01 plus 100
#ASSERT `would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100.01, FALSE) 0 500   -- 223.12: css 500, 100.01 is over 20 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE) 0 500))   -- 223.12: css 500, exactly 20 percent
-- A financial subsidiary is an affiliate for 223.12.
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Fin Sub", "Acme Fin Sub", 200, FALSE) 0 1000))   -- 223.12: a financial subsidiary, exactly 20 percent
#ASSERT `would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Fin Sub", "Acme Fin Sub", 200.01, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.12: a financial subsidiary is within the all-affiliates limit: a cent over
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Fin Sub", "Acme Fin Sub", 150, FALSE) 50 1000))   -- 223.12: a financial subsidiary, 150 plus 50
#ASSERT `would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Fin Sub", "Acme Fin Sub", 150, FALSE) 50.01 1000   -- 223.12: a financial subsidiary, 150 plus 50.01
#ASSERT `would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kSecurity, "Acme Mortgage Co", "Acme Mortgage Co", 200.01, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.12 applies to every covered kind: (h)(2) a purchase of a security
#ASSERT `would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Mortgage Co", "Acme Mortgage Co", 200.01, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.12 applies to every covered kind: (h)(3) a purchase of an asset
#ASSERT `would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAccept, "Acme Mortgage Co", "Acme Mortgage Co", 200.01, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.12 applies to every covered kind: (h)(4) acceptance of a security as collateral
#ASSERT `would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kGuarantee, "Acme Mortgage Co", "Acme Mortgage Co", 200.01, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.12 applies to every covered kind: (h)(5) a guarantee, acceptance or letter of credit
#ASSERT `would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kNetting, "Acme Mortgage Co", "Acme Mortgage Co", 200.01, FALSE) 0 1000   -- 223.12 applies to every covered kind: (h)(5) a cross-affiliate netting arrangement
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 5000, FALSE) 0 1000))   -- 223.12: a loan to a nonaffiliate is not a covered transaction
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kOther, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 5000, FALSE) 5000 1000))   -- 223.12: some other transaction is not covered
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the all-affiliates limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 5000, TRUE) 5000 1000))   -- 223.12: a Board-exempted purchase of property is not covered

§ `223.16(a) and (b): transactions with any person treated as transactions with an affiliate`

-- (a): a transaction with any person is treated as a transaction with an affiliate to the extent that the proceeds are used for the benefit of,
-- or transferred to, an affiliate.
-- (b)(1): an extension of credit to a nonaffiliate is NOT so treated if (i) the proceeds buy an asset through an affiliate acting exclusively as agent or broker
-- and (ii) the asset is not issued, underwritten or sold as principal by any affiliate; (b)(2): but it is so treated to the extent of any agency fee,
-- brokerage commission or other compensation an affiliate receives from the proceeds.
-- Use of proceeds OF amount used for the benefit of, or transferred to, an affiliate; bought through an affiliate acting exclusively as agent or broker;
-- asset not issued, underwritten or sold as principal by any affiliate; fee or commission an affiliate receives from the proceeds.
-- The transaction is a loan of 1000 to Stranger Corp unless stated.
#ASSERT `amount treated as a transaction with an affiliate` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 1000, FALSE) (`Use of proceeds` OF 1000, FALSE, FALSE, 0) EQUALS 1000   -- (a): all 1000 of the proceeds go to an affiliate: the whole loan is treated as with an affiliate
#ASSERT `amount treated as a transaction with an affiliate` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 1000, FALSE) (`Use of proceeds` OF 400, FALSE, FALSE, 0) EQUALS 400   -- (a): only 400 of 1000 goes to an affiliate: treated as with an affiliate to that extent
#ASSERT `amount treated as a transaction with an affiliate` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 1000, FALSE) (`Use of proceeds` OF 1, FALSE, FALSE, 0) EQUALS 1   -- (a): to the extent: 1 of 1000
#ASSERT `amount treated as a transaction with an affiliate` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 1000, FALSE) (`Use of proceeds` OF 0, FALSE, FALSE, 0) EQUALS 0   -- (a): none of the proceeds goes to an affiliate: nothing is treated as with an affiliate
#ASSERT `amount treated as a transaction with an affiliate` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 1000, FALSE) (`Use of proceeds` OF 1000, TRUE, FALSE, 0) EQUALS 1000   -- (b)(1)(ii) fails alone: the asset is sold as principal by an affiliate: (b) does not help
#ASSERT `amount treated as a transaction with an affiliate` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 1000, FALSE) (`Use of proceeds` OF 1000, FALSE, TRUE, 0) EQUALS 1000   -- (b)(1)(i) fails alone: the affiliate is not acting exclusively as agent or broker: (b) does not help
#ASSERT `amount treated as a transaction with an affiliate` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 1000, FALSE) (`Use of proceeds` OF 1000, TRUE, TRUE, 20) EQUALS 20   -- (b)(1) and (b)(2): both limbs hold, so only the 20 commission is treated as with an affiliate
#ASSERT `amount treated as a transaction with an affiliate` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 1000, FALSE) (`Use of proceeds` OF 1000, TRUE, TRUE, 0) EQUALS 0   -- (b)(1): both limbs hold and no commission: nothing is treated as with an affiliate
#ASSERT `amount treated as a transaction with an affiliate` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 1000, FALSE) (`Use of proceeds` OF 1000, TRUE, TRUE, 1) EQUALS 1   -- (b)(2): the smallest commission
#ASSERT `amount treated as a transaction with an affiliate` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 1000, FALSE) (`Use of proceeds` OF 500, TRUE, TRUE, 10) EQUALS 10   -- (b)(2): proceeds of 500 used through an agent, commission 10
#ASSERT `amount treated as a transaction with an affiliate` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 1000, FALSE) (`Use of proceeds` OF 1000, FALSE, FALSE, 20) EQUALS 1000   -- (a): a commission figure changes nothing when (b)(1) does not apply
#ASSERT `amount treated as a transaction with an affiliate` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 1000, FALSE) (`Use of proceeds` OF 1000, TRUE, FALSE, 20) EQUALS 1000   -- (b)(1)(ii) fails alone, with a commission: the whole 1000 is still treated as with an affiliate
#ASSERT `amount treated as a transaction with an affiliate` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 1000, FALSE) (`Use of proceeds` OF 1000, FALSE, TRUE, 20) EQUALS 1000   -- (b)(1)(i) fails alone, with a commission: the whole 1000
#ASSERT `amount treated as a transaction with an affiliate` (Transaction OF kGuarantee, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 1000, FALSE) (`Use of proceeds` OF 1000, TRUE, TRUE, 20) EQUALS 1000   -- (b)(1) speaks only of an extension of credit: a guarantee is not within it
-- The worked example of 223.24(c)(3): a loan of 100 to a nonaffiliate, the bank knows all the proceeds buy securities issued by an affiliate (eligible mutual fund shares).
#ASSERT `amount treated as a transaction with an affiliate` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 100, FALSE) (`Use of proceeds` OF 100, FALSE, FALSE, 0) EQUALS 100   -- 223.24(c)(3) example: the loan is treated as a loan to an affiliate

§ `223.16(c): exemptions from the limits and the collateral requirements`

-- (c)(2): retention of a brokerage commission, agency fee or riskless principal mark-up described in (b) or (c)(1), if it is substantially the same as,
-- or lower than, those prevailing for comparable transactions with other nonaffiliates (the market terms standard).
#ASSERT `exempt as a commission, fee or mark-up on market terms` TRUE TRUE   -- (c)(2): every condition satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a commission, fee or mark-up on market terms` FALSE TRUE))   -- (c)(2): only retentionIsOfCommissionFeeOrMarkup is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a commission, fee or mark-up on market terms` TRUE FALSE))   -- (c)(2): only onMarketTerms is not satisfied
-- (c)(1): an extension of credit to a nonaffiliate, if (i) the proceeds buy a security through a securities affiliate acting exclusively as a riskless principal, (ii) the security is not issued, underwritten or sold as principal (other than riskless principal) by any affiliate, and (iii) any riskless principal mark-up meets the market terms standard of (c)(2).
#ASSERT `exempt as a riskless principal credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE   -- (c)(1): every condition satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a riskless principal credit` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))   -- (c)(1): only extensionToANonaffiliate is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a riskless principal credit` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE))   -- (c)(1): only securityBoughtThroughSecuritiesAffiliateAsRisklessPrincipal is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a riskless principal credit` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))   -- (c)(1): only securityNotIssuedUnderwrittenOrSoldAsPrincipalByAnAffiliate is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a riskless principal credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))   -- (c)(1): only compensationMeetsMarketTerms is not satisfied
-- (c)(3): an extension of credit to a nonaffiliate, if (i) the proceeds buy a security from or through a securities affiliate and (ii) it is made under a preexisting line of credit, consistent with its conditions, that was not established in contemplation of the purchase.
#ASSERT `exempt as a credit under a preexisting line` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE   -- (c)(3): every condition satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a credit under a preexisting line` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))   -- (c)(3): only extensionToANonaffiliate is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a credit under a preexisting line` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE))   -- (c)(3): only proceedsBuySecurityFromOrThroughASecuritiesAffiliate is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a credit under a preexisting line` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))   -- (c)(3): only madeUnderAPreexistingLineConsistentWithItsConditions is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a credit under a preexisting line` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))   -- (c)(3): only lineNotEstablishedInContemplationOfThePurchase is not satisfied
-- (c)(4)(ii): a general purpose credit card is a card widely accepted by merchants that are not affiliates, if
-- (A) less than 25 percent of the total value of purchases with the card by all cardholders are purchases from affiliates; or
-- (B) all affiliates would be permissible for a financial holding company, and the bank has no reason to believe 25 percent or more are or would be purchases from affiliates; or
-- (C) the bank presents information to the Board that demonstrates to the Board's satisfaction that less than 25 percent are and would be.
-- Each case below satisfies exactly one of (A), (B), (C) unless stated.  Arguments: widely accepted; percent of purchases from affiliates; all affiliates permissible; no reason to believe 25 percent;
-- the Board accepted a showing.
#ASSERT `is a general purpose credit card` TRUE 24.99 FALSE FALSE FALSE   -- (A) alone: 24.99 percent is less than 25
#ASSERT `is a general purpose credit card` TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE   -- (A) alone: no purchases at all from affiliates
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a general purpose credit card` TRUE 25 FALSE FALSE FALSE))   -- (A) fails at exactly 25 percent: not LESS than 25, and neither (B) nor (C) holds
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a general purpose credit card` TRUE 27 FALSE FALSE FALSE))   -- 223.16(c)(4)(iv) example: 27 percent from an affiliate fails the 25 percent test (and neither (B) nor (C) holds)
#ASSERT `is a general purpose credit card` TRUE 40 TRUE TRUE FALSE   -- (B) alone: (A) is off at 40 percent, both limbs of (B) hold
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a general purpose credit card` TRUE 40 FALSE TRUE FALSE))   -- (B) fails: some affiliate is not permissible for a financial holding company
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a general purpose credit card` TRUE 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE))   -- (B) fails: the bank has reason to believe 25 percent or more
#ASSERT `is a general purpose credit card` TRUE 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE   -- (C) alone: the Board accepted a showing
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a general purpose credit card` TRUE 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE))   -- none of (A), (B), (C) holds at 40 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a general purpose credit card` FALSE 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE))   -- not widely accepted by nonaffiliate merchants, though (A) holds
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a general purpose credit card` FALSE 40 TRUE TRUE FALSE))   -- not widely accepted, though (B) holds
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a general purpose credit card` FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE))   -- not widely accepted, though (C) holds
#ASSERT `is a general purpose credit card` TRUE 10 TRUE TRUE TRUE   -- all of (A), (B), (C) hold
-- (c)(4)(i): an extension of credit to a nonaffiliate, if (A) the proceeds are used to buy a product or service from an affiliate and (B) the extension is made
-- under, and consistent with the conditions of, a general purpose credit card issued by the bank.  (c)(4)(iii): a card that qualified for 3 consecutive months and then ceases to qualify
-- may be treated as a general purpose credit card for that month and three more.
-- Arguments: extension to a nonaffiliate; proceeds buy from an affiliate; made under a general purpose credit card; the card qualifies; within the grace period.
#ASSERT `exempt as a general purpose credit card transaction` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE   -- (c)(4): every condition satisfied, the card qualifies
#ASSERT `exempt as a general purpose credit card transaction` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE   -- (c)(4)(iii): the card has stopped qualifying but is within the grace period
#ASSERT `exempt as a general purpose credit card transaction` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE   -- (c)(4): the card qualifies and the grace period is also running
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a general purpose credit card transaction` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))   -- (c)(4)(iii): the card does not qualify and the grace period has ended
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a general purpose credit card transaction` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))   -- (c)(4)(i): not an extension of credit to a nonaffiliate, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a general purpose credit card transaction` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE))   -- (c)(4)(i)(A): the proceeds do not buy from an affiliate, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a general purpose credit card transaction` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))   -- (c)(4)(i)(B): not made under a general purpose credit card, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a general purpose credit card transaction` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))   -- (c)(4)(i)(B): not under a general purpose credit card, even within a grace period
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a general purpose credit card transaction` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))   -- (c)(4)(i): not to a nonaffiliate, even within a grace period

§ `223.3(v): a low-quality asset`

-- (1) classified substandard, doubtful or loss, or treated as special mention or other transfer risk problems; (2) in nonaccrual status;
-- (3) principal or interest payments MORE THAN thirty days past due; (4) terms renegotiated or compromised because of deteriorating financial condition;
-- (5) acquired through foreclosure, repossession or otherwise in satisfaction of a debt, and not yet reviewed in an examination or inspection.
-- Asset condition OF classified or specially treated; in nonaccrual status; days past due; renegotiated because of deterioration; acquired in satisfaction of a debt and not yet reviewed.
#ASSERT `is a low-quality asset` (`Asset condition` OF TRUE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE)   -- (v)(1) alone: classified or specially treated
#ASSERT `is a low-quality asset` (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE)   -- (v)(2) alone: in nonaccrual status
#ASSERT `is a low-quality asset` (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, FALSE, 31, FALSE, FALSE)   -- (v)(3) alone: 31 days past due is more than thirty
#ASSERT `is a low-quality asset` (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, FALSE, 100, FALSE, FALSE)   -- (v)(3) alone: 100 days past due
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a low-quality asset` (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, FALSE)))   -- (v)(3): exactly thirty days past due is not MORE than thirty
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a low-quality asset` (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, FALSE, 29, FALSE, FALSE)))   -- (v)(3): 29 days past due
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a low-quality asset` (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, FALSE, 1, FALSE, FALSE)))   -- (v)(3): 1 day past due
#ASSERT `is a low-quality asset` (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, FALSE, 0, TRUE, FALSE)   -- (v)(4) alone: terms renegotiated because of deterioration
#ASSERT `is a low-quality asset` (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- (v)(5) alone: acquired in satisfaction of a debt and not yet reviewed
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a low-quality asset` (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE)))   -- none of (v)(1) to (5): a sound asset
#ASSERT `is a low-quality asset` (`Asset condition` OF TRUE, TRUE, 45, TRUE, TRUE)   -- every limb of (v) at once
#ASSERT `is a low-quality asset` (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 10, FALSE, FALSE)   -- (v)(2) with a small arrears figure
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a low-quality asset` (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE)))   -- no limb: zero days past due

§ `223.14: collateral requirements`

-- (b)(1): the collateral must have a market value of at least: 100 percent of the amount of the transaction if it is obligations of the United States or its agencies,
-- obligations fully guaranteed as to principal and interest by them, notes, drafts, bills of exchange or bankers' acceptances eligible for rediscount or purchase by a Federal Reserve Bank,
-- or a segregated earmarked deposit account; 110 percent if obligations of a State or political subdivision; 120 percent if other debt instruments, including loans and other receivables;
-- 130 percent if stock, leases, or other real or personal property.
#ASSERT `percent the collateral must stand at` cUS EQUALS 100   -- (b)(1)(i)(A) obligations of the United States or its agencies
#ASSERT `percent the collateral must stand at` cGuar EQUALS 100   -- (b)(1)(i)(B) obligations fully guaranteed by the United States or its agencies
#ASSERT `percent the collateral must stand at` cNotes EQUALS 100   -- (b)(1)(i)(C) notes, drafts, bills of exchange or bankers' acceptances eligible for rediscount
#ASSERT `percent the collateral must stand at` cDeposit EQUALS 100   -- (b)(1)(i)(D) a segregated, earmarked deposit account
#ASSERT `percent the collateral must stand at` cState EQUALS 110   -- (b)(1)(ii) obligations of a State or political subdivision
#ASSERT `percent the collateral must stand at` cDebt EQUALS 120   -- (b)(1)(iii) other debt instruments
#ASSERT `percent the collateral must stand at` cProp EQUALS 130   -- (b)(1)(iv) stock, leases, or other real or personal property
-- (c): ineligible collateral: (1) low-quality assets; (2) securities issued by any affiliate; (3) equity securities of the member bank and its debt securities that represent regulatory capital; (4) intangible assets (including servicing assets) unless the Board specifically approved; (5) guarantees, letters of credit and similar instruments.
#ASSERT `is eligible collateral` (`clean collateral` cUS 100)   -- eligible: obligations of the United States
#ASSERT `is eligible collateral` (`clean collateral` cGuar 100)   -- eligible: guaranteed obligations
#ASSERT `is eligible collateral` (`clean collateral` cNotes 100)   -- eligible: notes eligible for rediscount
#ASSERT `is eligible collateral` (`clean collateral` cDeposit 100)   -- eligible: a segregated deposit account
#ASSERT `is eligible collateral` (`clean collateral` cState 100)   -- eligible: State obligations
#ASSERT `is eligible collateral` (`clean collateral` cDebt 100)   -- eligible: other debt instruments
#ASSERT `is eligible collateral` (`clean collateral` cProp 100)   -- eligible: stock, leases or other property
#ASSERT (NOT (`is eligible collateral` (`clean collateral` cLow 100)))   -- ineligible: (c)(1) a low-quality asset
#ASSERT (NOT (`is eligible collateral` (`clean collateral` cAffSec 100)))   -- ineligible: (c)(2) a security issued by an affiliate
#ASSERT (NOT (`is eligible collateral` (`clean collateral` cOwnEq 100)))   -- ineligible: (c)(3) equity of the member bank or its regulatory-capital debt
#ASSERT (NOT (`is eligible collateral` (`clean collateral` cIntang 100)))   -- ineligible: (c)(4) an intangible asset, not approved
#ASSERT (NOT (`is eligible collateral` (`clean collateral` cGuarLC 100)))   -- ineligible: (c)(5) a guarantee, letter of credit or similar instrument
#ASSERT `is eligible collateral` (`board approved collateral` cIntang 100)   -- (c)(4): an intangible asset the Board specifically approved is eligible
#ASSERT (NOT (`is eligible collateral` (`board approved collateral` cLow 100)))   -- (c)(1): Board approval rescues only an intangible: a low-quality asset stays ineligible
#ASSERT (NOT (`is eligible collateral` (`board approved collateral` cAffSec 100)))   -- (c)(2): Board approval does not rescue a security issued by an affiliate
#ASSERT (NOT (`is eligible collateral` (`board approved collateral` cOwnEq 100)))   -- (c)(3): Board approval does not rescue the member bank's own equity
#ASSERT (NOT (`is eligible collateral` (`board approved collateral` cGuarLC 100)))   -- (c)(5): Board approval does not rescue a guarantee or letter of credit
#ASSERT `is eligible collateral` (`board approved collateral` cUS 100)   -- an eligible kind stays eligible when the Board has approved it
-- (d): perfection and priority.  (d)(2): the bank either obtains a first priority security interest or must deduct from the value of the collateral the LESSER of
-- (i) the amount of any security interest in it that is senior to the bank's, or (ii) the amount of any credit secured by it that is senior to the bank's.
-- Collateral OF kind, market value, senior security interest, senior credit, approved by the Board, perfected and enforceable.
#ASSERT `effective value of collateral` (`clean collateral` cUS 500) EQUALS 500   -- (d)(2): first priority: nothing to deduct
#ASSERT `effective value of collateral` (`clean collateral` cDebt 480) EQUALS 480   -- (d)(2): first priority, debt instruments
#ASSERT `effective value of collateral` (`encumbered collateral` cProp 3000 1000 1000) EQUALS 2000   -- (d)(3) example: real estate worth 3000 behind a prior 1000 lien: effective value 2000
#ASSERT `effective value of collateral` (`encumbered collateral` cProp 3000 3000 1000) EQUALS 2000   -- (d)(2): the senior security interest covers the whole parcel (3000) but secures 1000: the lesser, 1000, is deducted
#ASSERT `effective value of collateral` (`encumbered collateral` cProp 3000 400 1000) EQUALS 2600   -- (d)(2): the senior security interest is the lesser (400): 400 is deducted
#ASSERT `effective value of collateral` (`encumbered collateral` cProp 3000 0 1000) EQUALS 3000   -- (d)(2): no senior security interest: the lesser is 0, nothing is deducted
#ASSERT `effective value of collateral` (`encumbered collateral` cProp 3000 1000 0) EQUALS 3000   -- (d)(2): no senior credit: the lesser is 0, nothing is deducted
#ASSERT `effective value of collateral` (`encumbered collateral` cProp 3000 500 500) EQUALS 2500   -- (d)(2): equal senior figures: 500 deducted
#ASSERT `effective value of collateral` (`encumbered collateral` cUS 100 30 70) EQUALS 70   -- (d)(2): the lesser of 30 and 70 is deducted from 100
#ASSERT `effective value of collateral` (`encumbered collateral` cUS 100 70 30) EQUALS 70   -- (d)(2): the lesser of 70 and 30 is deducted from 100
-- (d)(3) example: a loan of 2000 secured by real estate worth 3000 behind a 1000 lien: effective value 2000; required 2000 x 130 percent = 2600; so 600 short.
#ASSERT `collateral value required` 2000 130 EQUALS 2600   -- (d)(3) example: 2000 x 130 percent = 2600
-- (b)(2) example: a loan of 1000; collateral of 500 in U.S. Treasury securities, 480 in corporate debt securities and 130 in real estate:
-- 500 of the loan is 100 percent secured, 400 is 120 percent secured and 100 is 130 percent secured: all 1000 is secured.
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 500), (`clean collateral` cDebt 480), (`clean collateral` cProp 130)) EQUALS 1000   -- (b)(2) example: 500 + 480/1.2 + 130/1.3 = 1000
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`encumbered collateral` cProp 3000 1000 1000)) TIMES 13 EQUALS 20000   -- (d)(3) example: effective value 2000 at 130 percent secures 2000/1.3 of the loan (times 13 is 20000)
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 100)) EQUALS 100   -- collateral of 100 at 100 percent secures 100 of the transaction
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cGuar 100)) EQUALS 100   -- collateral of 100 at 100 percent secures 100 of the transaction
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cNotes 100)) EQUALS 100   -- collateral of 100 at 100 percent secures 100 of the transaction
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cDeposit 100)) EQUALS 100   -- collateral of 100 at 100 percent secures 100 of the transaction
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cState 110)) EQUALS 100   -- collateral of 110 at 110 percent secures 100 of the transaction
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cDebt 120)) EQUALS 100   -- collateral of 120 at 120 percent secures 100 of the transaction
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cProp 130)) EQUALS 100   -- collateral of 130 at 130 percent secures 100 of the transaction
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cState 55)) EQUALS 50   -- 110 percent: 55 secures 50
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cDebt 60)) EQUALS 50   -- 120 percent: 60 secures 50
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cProp 65)) EQUALS 50   -- 130 percent: 65 secures 50
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 50), (`clean collateral` cDebt 60)) EQUALS 100   -- 50 at 100 percent plus 60 at 120 percent secure 50 + 50
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 25), (`clean collateral` cGuar 25), (`clean collateral` cNotes 25), (`clean collateral` cDeposit 25)) EQUALS 100   -- four kinds at 100 percent, 25 each
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cDebt 120), (`clean collateral` cDebt 120)) EQUALS 200   -- two pieces of debt collateral add
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 50), (`clean collateral` cAffSec 500)) EQUALS 50   -- (c)(2): the affiliate's securities add nothing
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 50), (`clean collateral` cLow 500), (`clean collateral` cOwnEq 500), (`clean collateral` cIntang 500), (`clean collateral` cGuarLC 500)) EQUALS 50   -- (c): every ineligible kind adds nothing
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 50), (`unperfected collateral` cUS 70)) EQUALS 50   -- (d)(1): a security interest that is not perfected and enforceable secures nothing
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cAffSec 500), (`clean collateral` cLow 500)) EQUALS 0   -- only ineligible collateral secures nothing
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` EMPTY EQUALS 0   -- no collateral secures nothing
#ASSERT `collateral value required` 1000 100 EQUALS 1000   -- 100 percent of 1000
#ASSERT `collateral value required` 1000 110 EQUALS 1100   -- 110 percent of 1000
#ASSERT `collateral value required` 1000 120 EQUALS 1200   -- 120 percent of 1000
#ASSERT `collateral value required` 1000 130 EQUALS 1300   -- 130 percent of 1000
#ASSERT `collateral value required` 500 110 EQUALS 550   -- 110 percent of 500
#ASSERT `collateral value required` 100 100 EQUALS 100   -- 100 percent of 100
-- (a) and (f): the collateral requirement attaches to each CREDIT transaction (223.3(i)); it does not attach to a purchase of an asset, a purchase of a security
-- or the acceptance of a security as collateral.  (f)(1): an acceptance already fully secured; (f)(2): the unused portion of an extension of credit while the bank has no legal obligation
-- to advance more until the required collateral for the whole used portion is provided; (f)(3): a debt security of an affiliate bought from a nonaffiliate in a bona fide secondary market.
-- Collateral exceptions OF acceptance already fully secured; unused portion; no obligation to advance until the required collateral is provided; debt security of an affiliate bought in the secondary market.
#ASSERT `amount that must be secured` kCredit 1000 `no exceptions` EQUALS 1000   -- (a): an extension of credit must be secured as to the whole transaction
#ASSERT `amount that must be secured` kGuarantee 500 `no exceptions` EQUALS 500   -- (a): a guarantee is a credit transaction
#ASSERT `amount that must be secured` kNetting 300 `no exceptions` EQUALS 300   -- (a): a cross-affiliate netting arrangement is a credit transaction
#ASSERT `amount that must be secured` kSecurity 1000 `no exceptions` EQUALS 0   -- (a): a purchase of a security is not a credit transaction
#ASSERT `amount that must be secured` kAsset 1000 `no exceptions` EQUALS 0   -- (a): a purchase of an asset is not a credit transaction
#ASSERT `amount that must be secured` kAccept 1000 `no exceptions` EQUALS 0   -- (a): accepting a security as collateral is not a credit transaction
#ASSERT `amount that must be secured` kGuarantee 500 (`Collateral exceptions` OF TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS 0   -- (f)(1): an acceptance already fully secured needs no collateral
#ASSERT `amount that must be secured` kCredit 300 (`Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 200, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS 100   -- (f)(2) with the revolver: a facility of 300, 200 unused, no obligation to advance until collateralised: only the used 100 must be secured
#ASSERT `amount that must be secured` kCredit 300 (`Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 200, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS 300   -- (f)(2) fails alone: the bank is obliged to advance, so the unused portion is not excepted
#ASSERT `amount that must be secured` kCredit 300 (`Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 0, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS 300   -- (f)(2): nothing is unused, so nothing is excepted
#ASSERT `amount that must be secured` kCredit 300 (`Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 50, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS 250   -- (f)(2): 50 unused
#ASSERT `amount that must be secured` kCredit 300 (`Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 300, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS 0   -- (f)(2): the whole facility is unused
#ASSERT `amount that must be secured` kGuarantee 300 (`Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 200, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS 300   -- (f)(2) concerns an extension of credit: a guarantee has no unused portion to except
#ASSERT `amount that must be secured` kCredit 100 (`Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 0, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS 0   -- (f)(3): a debt security of an affiliate bought from a nonaffiliate in the secondary market
#ASSERT `amount that must be secured` kCredit 100 (`Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS 100   -- (f)(3) does not apply: the same credit, not a secondary-market purchase
-- Whether the collateral requirement is met.  Arguments: kind of transaction, its value, the exceptions, the collateral.
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 1000 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 500), (`clean collateral` cDebt 480), (`clean collateral` cProp 130))   -- (b)(2) example: a loan of 1000 secured by 500 Treasuries, 480 corporate debt and 130 real estate satisfies the section
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 2000 `no exceptions` (LIST (`encumbered collateral` cProp 3000 1000 1000))))   -- (d)(3) example: a loan of 2000, real estate 3000 behind a 1000 lien: effective value 2000 is 600 short of 2600
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 2000 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cProp 2600))   -- (d)(3) with a first lien: real estate of exactly 2600 is 130 percent of 2000
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 2000 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cProp 2599.99))))   -- (d)(3): a cent under 130 percent of 2000
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 2000 `no exceptions` (LIST (`encumbered collateral` cProp 3600 1000 1000))   -- (d)(2): 3600 less the 1000 senior lien is exactly 2600
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 2000 `no exceptions` (LIST (`encumbered collateral` cProp 3599.99 1000 1000))))   -- (d)(2): a cent short after the senior lien
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 100))   -- loan of 100: exactly 100 percent, obligations of the United States
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 99.99))))   -- loan of 100: a cent under 100 percent, obligations of the United States
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cGuar 100))   -- loan of 100: exactly 100 percent, guaranteed obligations
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cGuar 99.99))))   -- loan of 100: a cent under 100 percent, guaranteed obligations
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cNotes 100))   -- loan of 100: exactly 100 percent, notes eligible for rediscount
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cNotes 99.99))))   -- loan of 100: a cent under 100 percent, notes eligible for rediscount
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cDeposit 100))   -- loan of 100: exactly 100 percent, a segregated deposit
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cDeposit 99.99))))   -- loan of 100: a cent under 100 percent, a segregated deposit
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cState 110))   -- loan of 100: exactly 110 percent, State obligations
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cState 109.99))))   -- loan of 100: a cent under 110 percent, State obligations
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cDebt 120))   -- loan of 100: exactly 120 percent, debt instruments
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cDebt 119.99))))   -- loan of 100: a cent under 120 percent, debt instruments
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cProp 130))   -- loan of 100: exactly 130 percent, property
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cProp 129.99))))   -- loan of 100: a cent under 130 percent, property
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 50), (`clean collateral` cDebt 60))   -- mixed: 50 at 100 percent and 60 at 120 percent cover 100
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 50), (`clean collateral` cDebt 59.99))))   -- mixed: a cent short on the debt collateral
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`unperfected collateral` cUS 100))))   -- (d)(1): the interest is not perfected and enforceable, so the bank is not secured
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`unperfected collateral` cUS 100), (`clean collateral` cUS 99.99))))   -- (d)(1): only the perfected 99.99 counts
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`unperfected collateral` cUS 100), (`clean collateral` cUS 100))   -- (d)(1): the perfected 100 suffices, the unperfected piece adds nothing
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cAffSec 1000))))   -- ineligible collateral, however large: (c)(2) a security of an affiliate
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cLow 1000))))   -- ineligible collateral, however large: (c)(1) a low-quality asset
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cOwnEq 1000))))   -- ineligible collateral, however large: (c)(3) the bank's own equity
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cIntang 1000))))   -- ineligible collateral, however large: (c)(4) an intangible asset
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cGuarLC 1000))))   -- ineligible collateral, however large: (c)(5) a guarantee or letter of credit
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cAffSec 1000), (`clean collateral` cUS 99.99))))   -- ineligible collateral does not make up a shortfall
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cAffSec 1000), (`clean collateral` cUS 100))   -- eligible 100 suffices; the ineligible 1000 is simply ignored
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kAsset 500 `no exceptions` EMPTY   -- (a): a purchase of an asset needs no collateral
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kSecurity 500 `no exceptions` EMPTY   -- (a): a purchase of a security needs no collateral
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kAccept 500 `no exceptions` EMPTY   -- (a): accepting a security as collateral needs no collateral
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` EMPTY))   -- (a): an extension of credit with no collateral
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kGuarantee 100 `no exceptions` EMPTY))   -- (a): a guarantee with no collateral
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kNetting 100 `no exceptions` EMPTY))   -- (a): a netting arrangement with no collateral
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 0 `no exceptions` EMPTY   -- a credit transaction of value 0 needs nothing
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kGuarantee 500 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cDeposit 500))   -- a guarantee of 500 secured by a segregated deposit of 500
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kNetting 300 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 300))   -- a netting arrangement of 300 secured by Treasuries of 300
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 300 (`Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 200, TRUE, FALSE) (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 100))   -- (f)(2) revolver: facility 300, 200 unused: Treasuries of 100 secure the used 100
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 300 (`Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 200, TRUE, FALSE) (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 99.99))))   -- (f)(2) revolver: a cent under 100 percent of the used 100
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 300 (`Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 200, TRUE, FALSE) (LIST (`clean collateral` cProp 130))   -- (f)(2) revolver: property of 130 is 130 percent of the used 100
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 300 (`Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 200, TRUE, FALSE) (LIST (`clean collateral` cProp 129.99))))   -- (f)(2) revolver: a cent under 130 percent of the used 100
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 300 (`Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 200, TRUE, FALSE) (LIST (`clean collateral` cState 110))   -- (f)(2) revolver: State obligations of 110 are 110 percent of the used 100
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 300 (`Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 200, FALSE, FALSE) (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 100))))   -- (f)(2) fails alone: the bank must advance regardless, so all 300 must be secured and 100 is not enough
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 300 (`Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 200, FALSE, FALSE) (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 300))   -- no (f)(2) exception: Treasuries of 300 secure all 300
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kGuarantee 500 (`Collateral exceptions` OF TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) EMPTY   -- (f)(1): an acceptance already fully secured needs no collateral
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kGuarantee 500 `no exceptions` EMPTY))   -- (f)(1) does not apply: the same guarantee, not an acceptance already fully secured
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 (`Collateral exceptions` OF FALSE, 0, FALSE, TRUE) EMPTY   -- (f)(3): a debt security of an affiliate bought from a nonaffiliate in the secondary market
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` EMPTY))   -- (f)(3) does not apply: the same purchase, not bought in the secondary market

§ `223.15: low-quality assets`

-- (b)(3): the participating bank's share of the renewal or extension must not exceed its proportional share of the original transaction by more than 5 percent
-- (unless the appropriate Federal banking agency gave prior written approval).  The interface carries a switch for what "5 percent" is.
-- The cases below are the ones where the two readings agree; the cases where they differ are in `Contested readings` (R2).
-- Shares are percentages of the transaction (20 means 20 percent).  Arguments: the bank's share of the renewal, its proportional share of the original transaction, the reading.
#ASSERT `share is within the five percent allowance` 20 20 pp   -- (b)(3) percentage points: share equal to the proportional share
#ASSERT `share is within the five percent allowance` 21 20 pp   -- (b)(3) percentage points: share 21 against proportional 20 is within either reading
#ASSERT `share is within the five percent allowance` 15 20 pp   -- (b)(3) percentage points: share below the proportional share
#ASSERT `share is within the five percent allowance` 0 0 pp   -- (b)(3) percentage points: both zero
#ASSERT (NOT (`share is within the five percent allowance` 25.01 20 pp))   -- (b)(3) percentage points: share 25.01 against proportional 20 exceeds under either reading
#ASSERT (NOT (`share is within the five percent allowance` 50 20 pp))   -- (b)(3) percentage points: share 50 against proportional 20
#ASSERT (NOT (`share is within the five percent allowance` 5.01 0 pp))   -- (b)(3) percentage points: any share over 5 against proportional 0 exceeds under either reading
#ASSERT `share is within the five percent allowance` 20 20 rel   -- (b)(3) percent more: share equal to the proportional share
#ASSERT `share is within the five percent allowance` 21 20 rel   -- (b)(3) percent more: share 21 against proportional 20 is within either reading
#ASSERT `share is within the five percent allowance` 15 20 rel   -- (b)(3) percent more: share below the proportional share
#ASSERT `share is within the five percent allowance` 0 0 rel   -- (b)(3) percent more: both zero
#ASSERT (NOT (`share is within the five percent allowance` 25.01 20 rel))   -- (b)(3) percent more: share 25.01 against proportional 20 exceeds under either reading
#ASSERT (NOT (`share is within the five percent allowance` 50 20 rel))   -- (b)(3) percent more: share 50 against proportional 20
#ASSERT (NOT (`share is within the five percent allowance` 5.01 0 rel))   -- (b)(3) percent more: any share over 5 against proportional 0 exceeds under either reading
-- (b): the exemption for a renewal of, or extension of additional credit with respect to, a bank's participation in a loan to a nonaffiliate originated by an affiliate, if
-- (1) the loan was not a low-quality asset when the bank bought its participation;
-- (2) the renewal is approved, as necessary to protect the bank's investment, by the bank's board of directors or, if the originating affiliate is a depository institution, by (i) an executive committee of the board or
--     (ii) one or more senior management officials if (A) the board approved standards, (B) each renewal meets the standards and (C) the board periodically reviews the renewals and the standards;
-- (3) the bank's share is within the 5 percent allowance unless the Federal banking agency gave prior written approval; and
-- (4) the bank gave its Federal banking agency written notice not later than 20 days after consummation.
-- The baseline satisfies (2) by the board route alone, with share equal to proportional share and notice on day 20.
-- Participation renewal OF is such a renewal; loan was not low-quality when bought; board approved; originating affiliate is a depository institution; executive committee approved; senior officials approved;
-- board approved standards; each renewal meets standards; board reviews; bank's share; proportional share; agency prior written approval; days to notice.
#ASSERT `the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp   -- (b): every limb satisfied by the board route (pp)
#ASSERT `the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) rel   -- (b): every limb satisfied by the board route (rel)
#ASSERT (NOT (`the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp))   -- (b) preface: not a renewal or extension of a participation, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp))   -- (b)(1): the loan was already a low-quality asset when the participation was bought, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp))   -- (b)(2): no approval by anyone, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 21) pp))   -- (b)(4): notice on day 21 is later than 20 days, alone
#ASSERT `the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp   -- (b)(4): notice on day 20 is not later than 20 days
#ASSERT `the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 19) pp   -- (b)(4): notice on day 19
#ASSERT `the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 0) pp   -- (b)(4): notice on the day of consummation
#ASSERT (NOT (`the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 25.01, 20, FALSE, 20) pp))   -- (b)(3): share 25.01 against proportional 20, no agency approval, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 25.01, 20, FALSE, 20) rel))   -- (b)(3): share 25.01 against proportional 20, no agency approval, alone (other reading)
#ASSERT `the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 25.01, 20, TRUE, 20) pp   -- (b)(3): outside the allowance but the agency gave prior written approval
#ASSERT `the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 25.01, 20, TRUE, 20) rel   -- (b)(3): outside the allowance but the agency gave prior written approval (other reading)
#ASSERT `the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 21, 20, FALSE, 20) pp   -- (b)(3): share 21 against proportional 20, within the allowance on either reading
#ASSERT `the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 21, 20, FALSE, 20) rel   -- (b)(3): share 21 against proportional 20, within the allowance on either reading
-- (b)(2): the approval routes.  Board route alone is the baseline.  Executive committee and senior management routes are open only if the originating affiliate is a depository institution.
#ASSERT `the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp   -- (b)(2)(i): executive committee approved, originating affiliate is a depository institution
#ASSERT (NOT (`the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp))   -- (b)(2)(i): executive committee approved but the originating affiliate is not a depository institution, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp))   -- (b)(2): the originating affiliate is a depository institution but nobody approved
#ASSERT `the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp   -- (b)(2)(ii): senior management approved and (A), (B), (C) all hold
#ASSERT (NOT (`the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp))   -- (b)(2)(ii)(A) fails alone: the board did not approve standards
#ASSERT (NOT (`the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp))   -- (b)(2)(ii)(B) fails alone: this renewal does not meet the standards
#ASSERT (NOT (`the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp))   -- (b)(2)(ii)(C) fails alone: the board does not review
#ASSERT (NOT (`the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp))   -- (b)(2)(ii): senior management route but the originating affiliate is not a depository institution, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp))   -- (b)(2)(ii): the standards are in place but no senior official approved this renewal, alone
#ASSERT `the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp   -- (b)(2): the board approved and the originating affiliate is also a depository institution: the board route stands
#ASSERT `the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp   -- (b)(2)(i): the executive committee route suffices even when the senior-management route is incomplete
#ASSERT (NOT (`the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 21) pp))   -- (b)(4) fails alone on the executive committee route
#ASSERT (NOT (`the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp))   -- (b)(1) fails alone on the senior-management route
-- (a): a bank may not purchase a low-quality asset from an affiliate unless, pursuant to an independent credit evaluation, it had committed itself to purchase the asset
-- before the time the affiliate acquired it.  Arguments: structure, readings, transaction, the asset's condition, independent credit evaluation made,
-- committed before the affiliate acquired it, the participation renewal facts, the five percent reading.  The transaction is a purchase of an asset from Acme Holdings, value 50, unless stated.
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE `no renewal` pp   -- (a): a nonaccrual asset bought from an affiliate with no prior commitment
#ASSERT (NOT (`purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) TRUE TRUE `no renewal` pp))   -- (a): evaluated and committed before the affiliate acquired it: not prohibited
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) TRUE FALSE `no renewal` pp   -- (a): evaluated but not committed beforehand: prohibited
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE TRUE `no renewal` pp   -- (a): committed but no independent credit evaluation: prohibited
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF TRUE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE `no renewal` pp   -- (a) with (v)(1): a classified asset
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, FALSE, 31, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE `no renewal` pp   -- (a) with (v)(3): 31 days past due
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, FALSE, 0, TRUE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE `no renewal` pp   -- (a) with (v)(4): renegotiated because of deterioration
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, TRUE) FALSE FALSE `no renewal` pp   -- (a) with (v)(5): acquired in satisfaction of a debt and not yet reviewed
#ASSERT (NOT (`purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE `no renewal` pp))   -- (a): 30 days past due is not a low-quality asset, so nothing is prohibited
#ASSERT (NOT (`purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE `no renewal` pp))   -- (a): a sound asset may be purchased without any prior commitment
#ASSERT (NOT (`purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Stranger Corp", "Stranger Corp", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE `no renewal` pp))   -- (a): the same asset bought from a nonaffiliate is not within 223.15(a)
#ASSERT (NOT (`purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kNetting, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE `no renewal` pp))   -- (a): a netting arrangement is not a purchase of an asset
#ASSERT (NOT (`purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kOther, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE `no renewal` pp))   -- (a): some other transaction is not a purchase of an asset
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Mortgage Co", "Acme Mortgage Co", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE `no renewal` pp   -- (a): purchase from a sister company
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Sister Bank", "Acme Sister Bank", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE `no renewal` pp   -- (a): purchase from a sister bank (a depository institution affiliate)
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Fin Sub", "Acme Fin Sub", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE `no renewal` pp   -- (a): purchase from a financial subsidiary
-- (b): the renewal exception lifts the prohibition when every limb holds.
#ASSERT (NOT (`purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp))   -- (b): a nonaccrual participation, renewed with every limb of (b) satisfied: the prohibition does not apply
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 21) pp   -- (b)(4) fails alone: notice on day 21, so the prohibition applies
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp   -- (b)(1) fails alone: the loan was low-quality when the participation was bought
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp   -- (b)(2) fails alone: no approval
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (`Participation renewal` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 20) pp   -- (b) preface fails alone: the facts are not a renewal of a participation
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 25.01, 20, FALSE, 20) pp   -- (b)(3) fails alone: share 25.01 against proportional 20, no agency approval
#ASSERT (NOT (`purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 25.01, 20, TRUE, 20) pp))   -- (b)(3): share 25.01 against proportional 20 with the agency's prior written approval
#ASSERT (NOT (`purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) TRUE TRUE (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 21) pp))   -- (a) and (b) both lift: not prohibited
#ASSERT (NOT (`purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 20, 20, FALSE, 21) pp))   -- a sound asset with a failing renewal: nothing to prohibit

§ `223.21: valuation of credit transactions`

-- (a)(1): a credit transaction is initially valued at the GREATER of (i) the principal amount, (ii) the amount owed by the affiliate to the bank under it, or
-- (iii) the sum of (A) the amount provided to or on behalf of the affiliate and (B) any additional amount the bank could be required to provide.
-- Arguments: principal, owed, provided, additional.
#ASSERT `initial value of a credit transaction` 100 100 98 0 EQUALS 100   -- (a)(4)(i) term loan: principal 100, net proceeds 98 after a 2 fee: valued at 100
#ASSERT `initial value of a credit transaction` 100 100 100 200 EQUALS 300   -- (a)(4)(ii) revolver: 300 facility, 100 drawn: 100 provided plus 200 more the bank could be required to provide is 300
#ASSERT `initial value of a credit transaction` 300 100 100 200 EQUALS 300   -- (a)(4)(ii) revolver, taking the principal amount as the 300 commitment: still 300
#ASSERT `initial value of a credit transaction` 0 0 0 500 EQUALS 500   -- (a)(4)(iii) guarantee: 500 payable if the affiliate defaults: valued at 500
#ASSERT `initial value of a credit transaction` 500 0 0 500 EQUALS 500   -- (a)(4)(iii) guarantee, with the principal amount taken as 500: still 500
#ASSERT `initial value of a credit transaction` 100 50 40 20 EQUALS 100   -- (a)(1)(i) is the greatest: principal 100 against owed 50 and 40 + 20
#ASSERT `initial value of a credit transaction` 100 150 40 20 EQUALS 150   -- (a)(1)(ii) is the greatest: owed 150 against principal 100 and 40 + 20
#ASSERT `initial value of a credit transaction` 100 50 90 30 EQUALS 120   -- (a)(1)(iii) is the greatest: 90 + 30 against principal 100 and owed 50
#ASSERT `initial value of a credit transaction` 100 50 90 0 EQUALS 100   -- (a)(1): principal 100 beats provided 90
#ASSERT `initial value of a credit transaction` 10 20 30 40 EQUALS 70   -- (a)(1)(iii): 30 + 40 = 70 beats 10 and 20
#ASSERT `initial value of a credit transaction` 80 70 60 10 EQUALS 80   -- (a)(1)(i): principal 80 against 70 and 60 + 10 = 70
-- (a)(2): a credit transaction with an affiliate acquired from a nonaffiliate is valued at the sum of the consideration given (including liabilities assumed) and any additional amount the bank could be required to provide.
#ASSERT `initial value of an acquired credit transaction` 90 0 EQUALS 90   -- (a)(4)(iv) example: a loan with 100 outstanding principal bought for 90 is valued at 90
#ASSERT `initial value of an acquired credit transaction` 90 25 EQUALS 115   -- (a)(2): consideration 90 plus 25 more the bank could be required to provide
#ASSERT `initial value of an acquired credit transaction` 100 0 EQUALS 100   -- (a)(2): consideration 100
#ASSERT `initial value of an acquired credit transaction` 0 40 EQUALS 40   -- (a)(2): no consideration, 40 more the bank could be required to provide

§ `223.22: valuation of asset purchases`

-- (a)(1): initially valued at the total consideration given (including liabilities assumed); (a)(2) sends some purchases to other sections.
#ASSERT `rule that values an asset purchase` `An ordinary asset` EQUALS `223.22(a)(1): the consideration given`   -- (a)(1): an ordinary asset is valued at the consideration given
#ASSERT `rule that values an asset purchase` `An extension of credit to an affiliate` EQUALS `223.21: the credit transaction rules`   -- (a)(2)(i): a purchase from an affiliate of an extension of credit to an affiliate is valued under 223.21
#ASSERT `rule that values an asset purchase` `An extension of credit to an affiliate that is evidenced by a security issued by an affiliate` EQUALS `223.23: the security rules`   -- (a)(2)(i): unless the note evidencing the extension of credit is a security issued by an affiliate: then 223.23
#ASSERT `rule that values an asset purchase` `A security issued by an affiliate` EQUALS `223.23: the security rules`   -- (a)(2)(ii): a purchase of a security issued by an affiliate is valued under 223.23
#ASSERT `rule that values an asset purchase` `Securities of an affiliate transferred to the member bank, treated as an asset purchase under 223.31` EQUALS `223.31(b): not encoded here`   -- (a)(2)(iii): securities transferred to the bank treated as an asset purchase under 223.31 are valued under 223.31(b)
#ASSERT `rule that values an asset purchase` `A line of credit, revolving credit facility or similar arrangement for a nonaffiliate` EQUALS `223.22(a)(2)(iv): the consideration given plus the additional amount`   -- (a)(2)(iv): a line of credit, revolving credit facility or similar arrangement for a nonaffiliate: consideration plus the additional amount
#ASSERT `initial value of an asset purchase` 10000000 0 EQUALS 10000000   -- (c)(1) example: a pool of loans bought from an affiliate for 10 million cash: valued at 10 million
#ASSERT `initial value of an asset purchase` 0 50000 EQUALS 50000   -- (c)(2) example: real property worth 200,000 contributed, no cash, a 50,000 mortgage assumed: valued at 50,000
#ASSERT `initial value of an asset purchase` 30 20 EQUALS 50   -- (a)(1): 30 cash plus 20 of liabilities assumed
#ASSERT `initial value of an asset purchase` 100 0 EQUALS 100   -- (a)(1): cash only
#ASSERT `value of an asset purchase later` 10000000 6000000 TRUE EQUALS 4000000   -- (c)(1) example: the borrowers repay 6 million of the loans: the bank may value the transaction at 4 million
#ASSERT `value of an asset purchase later` 50000 0 TRUE EQUALS 50000   -- (c)(2) example: the bank retains the property but pays off the mortgage: still valued at 50,000
#ASSERT `value of an asset purchase later` 100 40 TRUE EQUALS 60   -- (a)(1): reduced for 40 of amortization or depreciation
#ASSERT `value of an asset purchase later` 100 0 TRUE EQUALS 100   -- (a)(1): still held, no reduction
#ASSERT `value of an asset purchase later` 50000 0 FALSE EQUALS 0   -- (c)(2) example: the bank sells the property: the transaction ceases to be a covered transaction, regardless of the mortgage
#ASSERT `value of an asset purchase later` 10000000 0 FALSE EQUALS 0   -- (b)(1): a purchase remains covered only as long as the bank holds the asset: sold
#ASSERT `value of an asset purchase later` 100 30 FALSE EQUALS 0   -- (b)(1): sold, with a reduction figure: still 0
-- (a)(2)(iv): a purchase from an affiliate of a line of credit for a nonaffiliate: consideration given plus any additional amount the bank could be required to provide to the borrower.
#ASSERT `initial value of a purchased line of credit` 1000 4000 EQUALS 5000   -- (a)(2)(iv): consideration 1000 plus 4000 the bank could be required to advance
#ASSERT `initial value of a purchased line of credit` 0 300 EQUALS 300   -- (a)(2)(iv): no consideration, 300 to advance
#ASSERT `initial value of a purchased line of credit` 250 0 EQUALS 250   -- (a)(2)(iv): consideration only

§ `223.23: purchases of and investments in securities issued by an affiliate`

-- (a)(1): valued at the GREATER of (i) the consideration given (including liabilities assumed), reduced to reflect amortization to the extent consistent with GAAP, or (ii) the carrying value.  Arguments: consideration, amortization, carrying value.
#ASSERT `value of a security of an affiliate` 600 0 600 EQUALS 600   -- (a)(2)(i) example: debt securities of a mortgage company bought for 600, initial carrying value 600: valued at 600
#ASSERT `value of a security of an affiliate` 100 0 100 EQUALS 100   -- (a)(2)(ii) example: shares bought for 100, initial carrying value 100: valued at 100
#ASSERT `value of a security of an affiliate` 100 0 40 EQUALS 100   -- (a)(2)(ii) example, going forward: the carrying value declines to 40: still valued at 100
#ASSERT `value of a security of an affiliate` 0 0 300 EQUALS 300   -- (a)(2)(iii) example: shares contributed for no consideration, carrying value 300: valued at 300
#ASSERT `value of a security of an affiliate` 0 0 500 EQUALS 500   -- (a)(2)(iii) example, going forward: the carrying value rises to 500: valued at 500
#ASSERT `value of a security of an affiliate` 1000 200 700 EQUALS 800   -- (a)(1)(i): consideration 1000 reduced by 200 of amortization is 800, above carrying value 700
#ASSERT `value of a security of an affiliate` 1000 200 900 EQUALS 900   -- (a)(1)(ii): carrying value 900 is above 1000 - 200
#ASSERT `value of a security of an affiliate` 1000 200 800 EQUALS 800   -- (a)(1): the two limbs equal
#ASSERT `value of a security of an affiliate` 500 0 450 EQUALS 500   -- (a)(1)(i): consideration above carrying value

§ `223.24: extensions of credit secured by affiliate securities`

-- (a): an extension of credit to a nonaffiliate secured EXCLUSIVELY by securities issued by an affiliate is valued at the LESSER of (1) its total value or (2) the fair market value of the pledged affiliate securities,
-- if the bank verifies that the securities meet the market quotation standard of 223.42(e) or the standards of 223.42(f)(1) and (5).  Arguments: total, fair market value, verified.
#ASSERT `value of credit secured only by affiliate securities` 100 60 TRUE EQUALS 60   -- (a): verified, fair market value 60 below the credit of 100: valued at 60
#ASSERT `value of credit secured only by affiliate securities` 100 150 TRUE EQUALS 100   -- (a): verified, fair market value above the credit: valued at the credit, 100
#ASSERT `value of credit secured only by affiliate securities` 100 100 TRUE EQUALS 100   -- (a): verified, equal
#ASSERT `value of credit secured only by affiliate securities` 100 60 FALSE EQUALS 100   -- (a)(2): the bank has not verified the market quotation, so only the total value, 100, applies
#ASSERT `value of credit secured only by affiliate securities` 100 0 FALSE EQUALS 100   -- (a)(2): unverified, worthless securities: still 100
#ASSERT `value of credit secured only by affiliate securities` 250 40 TRUE EQUALS 40   -- (a): verified, 40 of 250
-- (b): secured in part by affiliate securities and in part by nonaffiliate collateral: the LESSER of (1) the total value less the fair market value of the nonaffiliate collateral, or (2) the fair market value of the affiliate securities pledged, if verified.  Arguments: total, nonaffiliate collateral value, affiliate securities value, verified.
#ASSERT `value of credit secured partly by affiliate securities` 100 30 50 TRUE EQUALS 50   -- (b): total less nonaffiliate collateral is 70; affiliate securities 50 are lesser
#ASSERT `value of credit secured partly by affiliate securities` 100 30 90 TRUE EQUALS 70   -- (b): total less nonaffiliate collateral is 70; affiliate securities 90 are greater
#ASSERT `value of credit secured partly by affiliate securities` 100 30 70 TRUE EQUALS 70   -- (b): the two limbs equal
#ASSERT `value of credit secured partly by affiliate securities` 100 30 50 FALSE EQUALS 70   -- (b)(2): unverified, so only total less nonaffiliate collateral, 70, applies
#ASSERT `value of credit secured partly by affiliate securities` 100 0 50 TRUE EQUALS 50   -- (b): no nonaffiliate collateral: the lesser of 100 and 50
#ASSERT `value of credit secured partly by affiliate securities` 100 0 150 TRUE EQUALS 100   -- (b): no nonaffiliate collateral: the lesser of 100 and 150
#ASSERT `value of credit secured partly by affiliate securities` 500 200 100 TRUE EQUALS 100   -- (b): 500 - 200 = 300 against affiliate securities of 100
-- (c)(1): eligible affiliated mutual fund securities are not securities issued by an affiliate and are instead nonaffiliate collateral, UNLESS the bank knows or has reason to know that the proceeds will be used to
-- purchase the eligible mutual fund securities collateral or will otherwise be used for the benefit of or transferred to an affiliate.
-- Arguments: the securities are eligible affiliated mutual fund securities; the bank knows or has reason to know of the use of proceeds.
#ASSERT `pledged securities count as securities of an affiliate` FALSE FALSE   -- (c)(1): not eligible mutual fund securities: they are securities issued by an affiliate
#ASSERT `pledged securities count as securities of an affiliate` FALSE TRUE   -- (c)(1): not eligible, and the bank knows the use: still securities of an affiliate
#ASSERT (NOT (`pledged securities count as securities of an affiliate` TRUE FALSE))   -- (c)(1): eligible mutual fund securities and the bank has no reason to know of the use: nonaffiliate collateral
#ASSERT `pledged securities count as securities of an affiliate` TRUE TRUE   -- (c)(1) and (c)(3) example: eligible, but the bank knows the proceeds buy those very securities: securities of an affiliate
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cAffSec 100))))   -- (c)(3) example: a loan of 100 secured exclusively by the affiliate's mutual fund securities, which the bank knows were bought with the proceeds: they are securities of an affiliate, ineligible under 223.14(c)(2), so the loan does not comply with 223.14
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`clean collateral` cAffSec 100), (`clean collateral` cUS 100))   -- (c)(3) example, repaired: the same loan with 100 of Treasuries added complies
-- (c)(2): eligible affiliated mutual fund securities are securities of an affiliate that is an open-end investment company registered with the SEC, if (i) they meet the market quotation standard of 223.42(e),
-- or the standards of 223.42(f)(1) and (5), or have closing prices made public through a mutual fund supermarket website; and (ii) the bank and its affiliates do not own or control in the aggregate
-- more than 5 percent of any class of voting securities or of the equity capital of the investment company.
-- Arguments: registered open-end investment company; meets 42(e); meets 42(f)(1) and (5); public closing prices; percent of a class of voting securities held; percent of equity capital held.
-- Each case satisfies exactly one of the three alternatives of (i) unless stated.
#ASSERT `are eligible affiliated mutual fund securities` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 5   -- (c)(2)(i)(A) alone and exactly 5 percent of the class and of the equity capital
#ASSERT `are eligible affiliated mutual fund securities` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 5 5   -- (c)(2)(i)(B) alone
#ASSERT `are eligible affiliated mutual fund securities` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 5 5   -- (c)(2)(i)(C) alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`are eligible affiliated mutual fund securities` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 5 5))   -- none of (i)(A), (B), (C)
#ASSERT (NOT (`are eligible affiliated mutual fund securities` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 5))   -- not a registered open-end investment company, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`are eligible affiliated mutual fund securities` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 5))   -- not registered, though every alternative of (i) holds
#ASSERT (NOT (`are eligible affiliated mutual fund securities` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 5.01 5))   -- (c)(2)(ii): the bank and its affiliates hold 5.01 percent of a class, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`are eligible affiliated mutual fund securities` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 5 5.01))   -- (c)(2)(ii): the bank and its affiliates hold 5.01 percent of the equity capital, alone
#ASSERT `are eligible affiliated mutual fund securities` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 4.99 4.99   -- (c)(2)(ii): just under 5 percent of each
#ASSERT `are eligible affiliated mutual fund securities` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 0   -- (c)(2)(ii): no holdings
#ASSERT (NOT (`are eligible affiliated mutual fund securities` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 50 50))   -- (c)(2)(ii): half of the fund

§ `223.41: exemptions from the quantitative limits and the collateral requirements`

-- 223.41 transactions are not subject to 223.11, 223.12 or 223.14, but remain subject to 223.13 and the low-quality asset prohibition of 223.15 (see `The effects of an exemption`).
-- (a): transactions with a depository institution if the member bank controls 80 percent or more of the voting securities of the depository institution
-- OR the depository institution controls 80 percent or more of the voting securities of the member bank.
-- Arguments: the counterparty is a depository institution; percent of its voting securities the bank controls; percent of the bank's voting securities it controls.
#ASSERT `exempt as a parent or subsidiary institution` TRUE 80 0   -- (a): the bank controls exactly 80 percent of the institution (the first direction alone)
#ASSERT `exempt as a parent or subsidiary institution` TRUE 0 80   -- (a): the institution controls exactly 80 percent of the bank (the other direction alone)
#ASSERT `exempt as a parent or subsidiary institution` TRUE 100 100   -- (a): control in both directions
#ASSERT `exempt as a parent or subsidiary institution` TRUE 90 10   -- (a): 90 percent one way, 10 the other
#ASSERT `exempt as a parent or subsidiary institution` TRUE 10 90   -- (a): 10 percent one way, 90 the other
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a parent or subsidiary institution` TRUE 79.99 0))   -- (a): the bank controls 79.99 percent: a cent short
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a parent or subsidiary institution` TRUE 0 79.99))   -- (a): the institution controls 79.99 percent of the bank: short
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a parent or subsidiary institution` TRUE 79.99 79.99))   -- (a): 79.99 percent each way: neither reaches 80 (the percents are not added)
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a parent or subsidiary institution` TRUE 40 40))   -- (a): 40 percent each way
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a parent or subsidiary institution` TRUE 0 0))   -- (a): no control either way
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a parent or subsidiary institution` FALSE 80 0))   -- (a): 80 percent held but the counterparty is not a depository institution, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a parent or subsidiary institution` FALSE 0 100))   -- (a): 100 percent held the other way but the counterparty is not a depository institution
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a parent or subsidiary institution` FALSE 100 100))   -- (a): control both ways, not a depository institution
-- (b): transactions with a depository institution if the SAME company controls 80 percent or more of the voting securities of the member bank AND of the depository institution.
#ASSERT `exempt as an institution under the same holding company` TRUE 80 80   -- (b): the same company holds exactly 80 percent of each
#ASSERT `exempt as an institution under the same holding company` TRUE 100 100   -- (b): 100 percent of each
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an institution under the same holding company` TRUE 80 79.99))   -- (b): 79.99 percent of the institution, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an institution under the same holding company` TRUE 79.99 80))   -- (b): 79.99 percent of the bank, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an institution under the same holding company` TRUE 0 100))   -- (b): the company controls the institution but not the bank
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an institution under the same holding company` TRUE 100 0))   -- (b): the company controls the bank but not the institution
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an institution under the same holding company` FALSE 80 80))   -- (b): the counterparty is not a depository institution, alone
-- (c): purchasing a loan on a nonrecourse basis from an affiliated depository institution.  Arguments: a purchase of a loan; nonrecourse; from an affiliated depository institution.
#ASSERT `exempt as a nonrecourse loan purchase` TRUE TRUE TRUE   -- (c): every condition satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a nonrecourse loan purchase` FALSE TRUE TRUE))   -- (c): only purchaseOfALoan is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a nonrecourse loan purchase` TRUE FALSE TRUE))   -- (c): only nonrecourse is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a nonrecourse loan purchase` TRUE TRUE FALSE))   -- (c): only fromAnAffiliatedInstitution is not satisfied
-- (d): purchasing assets from an affiliate if (1) the purchase is part of an internal corporate reorganization of a holding company AND involves the transfer of all or substantially all of the shares or assets of an affiliate or of a division or department of an affiliate;
-- (2) written notice goes to the agency and the Board before consummation; (3) the top-tier holding company commits to cash contributions or repurchase; (4) it complies with the commitment; (5) a majority of the directors approves before consummation;
-- (6) the value of the transaction, aggregated with the other transactions under this exemption in the preceding 12 calendar months, is LESS THAN 10 percent of capital stock and surplus (or such higher amount, up to 25 percent, as the agency permits);
-- (7) the holding company and all its subsidiary member banks and depository institutions are well capitalized and well managed and would remain well capitalized.
-- Arguments: a purchase of assets from an affiliate; part of an internal reorganization; transfers all or substantially all; written notice before consummation; holding company committed; holding company complies;
-- majority of directors approves; aggregate value (this transaction with the others in the preceding 12 months); capital stock and surplus; percent permitted (10, or higher up to 25 if the agency permits); well capitalized and well managed.
#ASSERT `exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 99 1000 10 TRUE   -- (d): every condition satisfied; aggregate value 99 is under 10 percent of 1000
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 99 1000 10 TRUE))   -- (d) preface: not a purchase of assets from an affiliate, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 99 1000 10 TRUE))   -- (d)(1): not part of an internal corporate reorganization of a holding company, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 99 1000 10 TRUE))   -- (d)(1): does not involve the transfer of all or substantially all of the shares or assets, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 99 1000 10 TRUE))   -- (d)(2): no written notice before consummation, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 99 1000 10 TRUE))   -- (d)(3): the top-tier holding company made no commitment, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 99 1000 10 TRUE))   -- (d)(4): the holding company does not comply with its commitment, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 99 1000 10 TRUE))   -- (d)(5): a majority of the directors has not approved, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 99 1000 10 FALSE))   -- (d)(7): not all well capitalized and well managed, alone
#ASSERT `exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 99.99 1000 10 TRUE   -- (d)(6): 99.99 of 1000 is a cent under 10 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 1000 10 TRUE))   -- (d)(6): exactly 10 percent is not LESS than 10 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 100.01 1000 10 TRUE))   -- (d)(6): a cent over 10 percent
#ASSERT `exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 1000 10 TRUE   -- (d)(6): nothing aggregated
#ASSERT `exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 200 1000 25 TRUE   -- (d)(6): the agency permitted up to 25 percent: 200 of 1000 is under 25 percent
#ASSERT `exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 249.99 1000 25 TRUE   -- (d)(6): 249.99 is a cent under 25 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 250 1000 25 TRUE))   -- (d)(6): exactly 25 percent is not LESS than 25 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 250.01 1000 25 TRUE))   -- (d)(6): a cent over 25 percent
#ASSERT `exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 1000 15 TRUE   -- (d)(6): the agency permitted 15 percent: exactly 10 percent is under it
#ASSERT `exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 149.99 1000 15 TRUE   -- (d)(6): a cent under 15 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 150 1000 15 TRUE))   -- (d)(6): exactly 15 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10 100 10 TRUE))   -- (d)(6): capital stock and surplus 100: exactly 10 percent
#ASSERT `exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 9.99 100 10 TRUE   -- (d)(6): capital stock and surplus 100: a cent under 10 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an internal corporate reorganization` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 200 1000 25 TRUE))   -- (d)(1) fails alone even with the higher percent

§ `223.42: exemptions from the quantitative limits, collateral requirements and the low-quality asset prohibition`

-- 223.42 transactions are not subject to 223.11, 223.12, 223.14 or 223.15, but remain subject to 223.13.
-- (a): making a deposit in an affiliated depository institution or affiliated foreign bank that represents an ongoing, working balance maintained in the ordinary course of correspondent business.
#ASSERT `exempt as a correspondent banking deposit` TRUE TRUE   -- (a): every condition satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a correspondent banking deposit` FALSE TRUE))   -- (a): only inAnAffiliatedInstitutionOrForeignBank is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a correspondent banking deposit` TRUE FALSE))   -- (a): only ongoingWorkingBalanceInTheOrdinaryCourse is not satisfied
-- (b): giving immediate credit to an affiliate for uncollected items received in the ordinary course of business.
#ASSERT `exempt as credit for uncollected items` TRUE TRUE   -- (b): every condition satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as credit for uncollected items` FALSE TRUE))   -- (b): only immediateCreditToAnAffiliate is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as credit for uncollected items` TRUE FALSE))   -- (b): only forUncollectedItemsInTheOrdinaryCourse is not satisfied
-- (c): engaging in a credit transaction with an affiliate TO THE EXTENT that it is and remains secured by (i) obligations of the United States or its agencies, (ii) obligations fully guaranteed by them as to principal and interest, or
-- (iii) a segregated, earmarked deposit account.  (Notes eligible for rediscount, in 223.14(b)(1)(i)(C), and State obligations are NOT in this list.)
#ASSERT `is cash or government collateral` (`clean collateral` cUS 100)   -- (c)(1)(i) obligations of the United States or its agencies
#ASSERT `is cash or government collateral` (`clean collateral` cGuar 100)   -- (c)(1)(ii) obligations fully guaranteed by the United States or its agencies
#ASSERT `is cash or government collateral` (`clean collateral` cDeposit 100)   -- (c)(1)(iii) a segregated, earmarked deposit account
#ASSERT (NOT (`is cash or government collateral` (`clean collateral` cNotes 100)))   -- not cash or government collateral: notes eligible for rediscount are not in 223.42(c)(1) (though they are at 100 percent in 223.14)
#ASSERT (NOT (`is cash or government collateral` (`clean collateral` cState 100)))   -- not cash or government collateral: State obligations are not in 223.42(c)(1)
#ASSERT (NOT (`is cash or government collateral` (`clean collateral` cDebt 100)))   -- not cash or government collateral: other debt instruments
#ASSERT (NOT (`is cash or government collateral` (`clean collateral` cProp 100)))   -- not cash or government collateral: stock, leases or other property
#ASSERT (NOT (`is cash or government collateral` (`clean collateral` cLow 100)))   -- not cash or government collateral: a low-quality asset
#ASSERT (NOT (`is cash or government collateral` (`clean collateral` cAffSec 100)))   -- not cash or government collateral: a security issued by an affiliate
#ASSERT (NOT (`is cash or government collateral` (`clean collateral` cOwnEq 100)))   -- not cash or government collateral: the bank's own equity
#ASSERT (NOT (`is cash or government collateral` (`clean collateral` cIntang 100)))   -- not cash or government collateral: an intangible asset
#ASSERT (NOT (`is cash or government collateral` (`clean collateral` cGuarLC 100)))   -- not cash or government collateral: a guarantee or letter of credit
-- The worked example: a 100 non-amortizing term loan secured by Treasury securities with market value 50 and real estate with market value 75: the value of the covered transaction is 50; if the Treasuries fall to 45, the value becomes 55.
#ASSERT `exempt part of a credit transaction secured by cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 50), (`clean collateral` cProp 75)) EQUALS 50   -- (c)(2) example: the Treasuries (50) exempt 50 of the loan; the real estate exempts nothing
#ASSERT `exempt part of a credit transaction secured by cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 45), (`clean collateral` cProp 75)) EQUALS 45   -- (c)(2) example, going forward: the Treasuries fall to 45, so 45 is exempt
#ASSERT `exempt part of a credit transaction secured by cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 150)) EQUALS 100   -- (c)(1): the exemption is only to the extent of the transaction: Treasuries of 150 exempt 100
#ASSERT `exempt part of a credit transaction secured by cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 100)) EQUALS 100   -- (c)(1): Treasuries of exactly 100 exempt all 100
#ASSERT `exempt part of a credit transaction secured by cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 30), (`clean collateral` cDeposit 40)) EQUALS 70   -- (c)(1): Treasuries 30 and a segregated deposit 40 exempt 70
#ASSERT `exempt part of a credit transaction secured by cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`clean collateral` cGuar 60)) EQUALS 60   -- (c)(1)(ii): fully guaranteed obligations of 60 exempt 60
#ASSERT `exempt part of a credit transaction secured by cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 50), (`clean collateral` cState 30)) EQUALS 50   -- (c)(1): State obligations exempt nothing
#ASSERT `exempt part of a credit transaction secured by cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`clean collateral` cNotes 100)) EQUALS 0   -- (c)(1): notes eligible for rediscount are not in the list, so they exempt nothing
#ASSERT `exempt part of a credit transaction secured by cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`clean collateral` cProp 75)) EQUALS 0   -- (c)(1): real estate alone exempts nothing
#ASSERT `exempt part of a credit transaction secured by cash or government securities` 100 EMPTY EQUALS 0   -- (c)(1): no collateral, nothing exempt
#ASSERT `value of a credit transaction after the exemption for cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 50), (`clean collateral` cProp 75)) EQUALS 50   -- (c)(2) example: value of the covered transaction is 100 - 50 = 50
#ASSERT `value of a credit transaction after the exemption for cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 45), (`clean collateral` cProp 75)) EQUALS 55   -- (c)(2) example, going forward: the Treasuries fall to 45: the value rises to 55
#ASSERT `value of a credit transaction after the exemption for cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 100)) EQUALS 0   -- (c)(1): fully secured by Treasuries: the value is 0
#ASSERT `value of a credit transaction after the exemption for cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 150)) EQUALS 0   -- (c)(1): over-secured by Treasuries: the value is 0, not negative
#ASSERT `value of a credit transaction after the exemption for cash or government securities` 100 EMPTY EQUALS 100   -- (c)(1): no collateral: the whole 100 counts
#ASSERT `value of a credit transaction after the exemption for cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`clean collateral` cProp 75)) EQUALS 100   -- (c)(1): real estate is not in the list: the whole 100 counts
#ASSERT `value of a credit transaction after the exemption for cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`clean collateral` cNotes 100)) EQUALS 100   -- (c)(1): notes eligible for rediscount are not in the list: the whole 100 counts
#ASSERT `value of a credit transaction after the exemption for cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 30), (`clean collateral` cDeposit 40)) EQUALS 30   -- (c)(1): 70 exempt, 30 counts
-- (d): purchasing a security issued by any company engaged solely in providing services described in section 4(c)(1) of the Bank Holding Company Act.
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of securities of a servicing affiliate` TRUE TRUE   -- (d): every condition satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of securities of a servicing affiliate` FALSE TRUE))   -- (d): only purchaseOfASecurity is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of securities of a servicing affiliate` TRUE FALSE))   -- (d): only issuerEngagedSolelyInServicesDescribedInSection4c1 is not satisfied
-- (e): purchasing an asset having a readily identifiable and publicly available market quotation and purchased at or below the asset's current market quotation.
-- Arguments: quoted routinely in a widely disseminated publication; price paid; current market quotation.
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a liquid asset` TRUE 100 100   -- (e): quoted, bought at exactly the current quotation
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a liquid asset` TRUE 99.99 100   -- (e): bought a cent below the quotation
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a liquid asset` TRUE 0 100   -- (e): bought far below the quotation
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a liquid asset` TRUE 100.01 100))   -- (e): bought a cent above the quotation, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a liquid asset` TRUE 150 100))   -- (e): bought well above the quotation
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a liquid asset` FALSE 100 100))   -- (e): no readily identifiable and publicly available quotation, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a liquid asset` FALSE 50 100))   -- (e): not quoted, even bought well below the figure
-- (f): purchasing a security from a securities affiliate, if (1) it has a ready market; (2) it is eligible for a State member bank to purchase directly and recorded as a purchase of a security;
-- (3) it is not a low-quality asset; (4) the bank does not purchase it during an underwriting, or within 30 days of an underwriting, if an affiliate is an underwriter, unless it is purchased as part of an issue of obligations of the United States or its agencies;
-- (5) its price is quoted routinely on an unaffiliated electronic service, the price paid is at or below the current quotation, and the size does not cast material doubt on relying on the quotation; (6) the bank keeps records for two years.
-- Arguments: from a securities affiliate; ready market; eligible and recorded as a security; not a low-quality asset; an affiliate is an underwriter; bought during or within 30 days of the underwriting;
-- part of an issue of United States obligations; quoted on an unaffiliated electronic service; price paid; current quotation; size does not cast material doubt; records kept two years.
-- The baseline has no affiliate underwriter, so (f)(4) is satisfied by the absence of an underwriting.
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 100 TRUE TRUE   -- (f): every condition satisfied, no underwriting, bought at exactly the quotation
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 100 TRUE TRUE))   -- (f) preface: not bought from a securities affiliate, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 100 TRUE TRUE))   -- (f)(1): no ready market, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 100 TRUE TRUE))   -- (f)(2): not eligible for a State member bank or not recorded as a purchase of a security, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 100 TRUE TRUE))   -- (f)(3): the security is a low-quality asset, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 100 TRUE TRUE))   -- (f)(5): not quoted on an unaffiliated electronic service, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 100 FALSE TRUE))   -- (f)(5)(ii): the size casts material doubt on the quotation, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 100 TRUE FALSE))   -- (f)(6): records not kept for two years, alone
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 99.99 100 TRUE TRUE   -- (f)(5)(i): a cent below the quotation
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100.01 100 TRUE TRUE))   -- (f)(5)(i): a cent above the quotation, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 100 100 TRUE TRUE))   -- (f)(4) fails alone: an affiliate underwrote it and the bank bought it during or within 30 days of the underwriting
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 100 TRUE TRUE   -- (f)(4): an affiliate underwrote it but the bank bought it more than 30 days after
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 100 100 TRUE TRUE   -- (f)(4): bought during an underwriting in which no affiliate is an underwriter
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 100 TRUE TRUE   -- (f)(4) carve-out: bought during an affiliate's underwriting but as part of an issue of United States obligations
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 100 TRUE FALSE))   -- (f)(4) carve-out does not excuse (f)(6)
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 100 TRUE TRUE   -- (f)(4): a United States issue with no underwriting problem
-- (g): purchasing a municipal security from a securities affiliate if (1) the security is rated by a nationally recognized statistical rating organization OR is part of an issue that does not exceed $25 million;
-- (2) it is eligible for a State member bank to purchase and recorded as a purchase of a security; and (3) the price is supported by ONE of (i) an unaffiliated electronic service (price at or below the current quotation, size not casting material doubt),
-- (ii) two or more actual current quotes from unaffiliated broker-dealers, based on a transaction similar in size, with the price paid no higher than the average of the quotes, or
-- (iii) the syndicate manager's written summary: bought during the underwriting at or below the summary price, and the bank keeps a copy for three years.
-- Arguments: from a securities affiliate; rated; size of the issue; eligible and recorded; quoted on an unaffiliated electronic service; price paid; current quotation; size does not cast material doubt;
-- two or more quotes from unaffiliated broker-dealers; quotes based on a similar size; average of the quotes; bought during the underwriting at or below the summary price; copy of the summary kept three years.
-- Each baseline satisfies exactly one of the three pricing limbs and has the other two off.
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE TRUE 100 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE   -- (g)(3)(i) alone: electronic service, price at the quotation; rated, so (g)(1) holds although the issue is over 25 million
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` FALSE TRUE 30000000 TRUE TRUE 100 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE))   -- (g) preface: not bought from a securities affiliate, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 FALSE TRUE 100 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE))   -- (g)(2): not eligible or not recorded as a purchase of a security, alone
-- (g)(1): rated, OR part of an issue not exceeding 25 million.
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE FALSE 25000000 TRUE TRUE 100 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE   -- (g)(1): not rated but the issue is exactly 25 million, which does not exceed 25 million
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE FALSE 24999999 TRUE TRUE 100 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE   -- (g)(1): not rated, the issue is 24,999,999
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE FALSE 25000001 TRUE TRUE 100 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE))   -- (g)(1) fails alone: not rated and the issue exceeds 25 million by 1
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 25000001 TRUE TRUE 100 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE   -- (g)(1): rated, so the size of the issue does not matter
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE FALSE 100000000 TRUE TRUE 100 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE))   -- (g)(1): not rated and a 100 million issue
-- (g)(3)(i): the electronic-service limb.
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE TRUE 99.99 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE   -- (g)(3)(i)(A): a cent below the quotation
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE TRUE 100.01 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE))   -- (g)(3)(i)(A) fails alone: a cent above the quotation (and the other limbs are off)
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE FALSE 100 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE))   -- (g)(3)(i): not quoted on an unaffiliated electronic service, and no other limb
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE TRUE 100 100 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE))   -- (g)(3)(i)(B) fails alone: the size casts material doubt on the quotation
-- (g)(3)(ii): the broker-dealer quotes limb alone (limb (i) off because the security is not quoted on an electronic service).
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE FALSE 100 100 TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 FALSE FALSE   -- (g)(3)(ii) alone: two quotes of similar size, price paid 100 is no higher than the average 100
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE FALSE 99.99 100 TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 FALSE FALSE   -- (g)(3)(ii): a cent below the average of the quotes
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE FALSE 100.01 100 TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 FALSE FALSE))   -- (g)(3)(ii)(B) fails alone: a cent above the average of the quotes
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE FALSE 100 90 TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 FALSE FALSE   -- (g)(3)(ii): the yardstick is the average of the broker-dealer quotes (100), not the electronic quotation (90, which does not matter here)
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE FALSE 100 110 TRUE TRUE TRUE 90 FALSE FALSE))   -- (g)(3)(ii)(B) fails alone: price paid 100 is above the average of the quotes, 90, though below the electronic quotation, 110
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE FALSE 100 100 TRUE FALSE TRUE 100 FALSE FALSE))   -- (g)(3)(ii) fails alone: fewer than two quotes
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE FALSE 100 100 TRUE TRUE FALSE 100 FALSE FALSE))   -- (g)(3)(ii)(A) fails alone: the quotes are not based on a transaction similar in size
-- (g)(3)(iii): the syndicate-summary limb alone (limbs (i) and (ii) off).
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE FALSE 100 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE   -- (g)(3)(iii) alone: bought during the underwriting at or below the summary price, summary kept three years
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE FALSE 100 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE))   -- (g)(3)(iii)(A) fails alone: not bought during the underwriting at or below the summary price
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE FALSE 100 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE))   -- (g)(3)(iii)(B) fails alone: no copy of the summary obtained and kept three years
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE FALSE 25000001 TRUE FALSE 100 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE))   -- (g)(1) fails alone on the summary limb
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE FALSE 100 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE))   -- (g)(3): none of the three pricing limbs holds
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` TRUE TRUE 30000000 TRUE FALSE 100 100 FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 FALSE FALSE   -- (g)(3)(ii): the size-doubt condition belongs to limb (i) only, so limb (ii) alone still suffices when it is false
-- (h): purchasing from an affiliate an extension of credit that was originated by the member bank and sold to the affiliate subject to a repurchase agreement or with recourse.
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase subject to a repurchase agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE   -- (h): every condition satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase subject to a repurchase agreement` FALSE TRUE TRUE))   -- (h): only purchaseFromAnAffiliate is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase subject to a repurchase agreement` TRUE FALSE TRUE))   -- (h): only originatedByTheMemberBank is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase subject to a repurchase agreement` TRUE TRUE FALSE))   -- (h): only soldSubjectToRepurchaseOrWithRecourse is not satisfied
-- (i): the purchase of an asset from an affiliate by a newly formed member bank, if the agency approved the purchase in writing in connection with its review of the formation.
#ASSERT `exempt as an asset purchase by a newly formed member bank` TRUE TRUE   -- (i): every condition satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an asset purchase by a newly formed member bank` FALSE TRUE))   -- (i): only byANewlyFormedMemberBank is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an asset purchase by a newly formed member bank` TRUE FALSE))   -- (i): only approvedInWritingOnReviewOfTheFormation is not satisfied
-- (j): a merger, consolidation, acquisition of assets or assumption of deposit liabilities with an affiliated depository institution or U.S. branch or agency of a foreign bank, if approved under the Bank Merger Act.
#ASSERT `exempt as a transaction approved under the Bank Merger Act` TRUE TRUE   -- (j): every condition satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a transaction approved under the Bank Merger Act` FALSE TRUE))   -- (j): only mergerOrAcquisitionWithAnAffiliatedInstitutionOrBranch is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a transaction approved under the Bank Merger Act` TRUE FALSE))   -- (j): only approvedUnderTheBankMergerAct is not satisfied
-- (k): purchasing from an affiliate, on a nonrecourse basis, an extension of credit, if (1) the affiliate originated it; (2) the bank independently evaluated the borrower's creditworthiness before the affiliate made or committed to make it;
-- (3) the bank committed to purchase it before then; (4) the bank has no blanket advance commitment; (5) its dollar amount, aggregated with the other extensions of credit the bank and its depository institution affiliates purchased from the affiliate in the preceding 12 months,
-- is not MORE THAN 50 percent (or such lower percent as the agency imposes) of the extensions of credit the affiliate originated in the preceding 12 months.
-- Arguments: nonrecourse; originated by the affiliate; independent evaluation beforehand; committed beforehand; no blanket advance commitment; this amount; other purchases in the preceding year; originated in the preceding year (including this one); percent allowed (50, or lower).
#ASSERT `exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 300 1000 50   -- (k): every condition satisfied; 100 + 300 = 400 is 40 percent of 1000
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 300 1000 50))   -- (k) preface: not on a nonrecourse basis, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 300 1000 50))   -- (k)(1): not originated by the affiliate, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 300 1000 50))   -- (k)(2): no independent evaluation before the affiliate made or committed to the credit, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 100 300 1000 50))   -- (k)(3): the bank did not commit to purchase beforehand, alone
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 100 300 1000 50))   -- (k)(4): the bank made a blanket advance commitment, alone
#ASSERT `exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 200 300 1000 50   -- (k)(5): 200 + 300 = 500 is exactly 50 percent of 1000
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 200.01 300 1000 50))   -- (k)(5): 200.01 + 300 is a cent over 50 percent
#ASSERT `exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 500 0 1000 50   -- (k)(5): this purchase alone is exactly 50 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 500.01 0 1000 50))   -- (k)(5): this purchase alone, a cent over 50 percent
#ASSERT `exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 500 1000 50   -- (k)(5): others alone exactly 50 percent
#ASSERT `exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 300 1000 40   -- (k)(5): the agency imposed a lower percent, 40: 400 of 1000 is exactly 40 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 100.01 300 1000 40))   -- (k)(5): the lower percent, 40: a cent over
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 300 1000 39.99))   -- (k)(5): a lower percent, 39.99: 400 of 1000 exceeds it
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 0 0 50))   -- (k)(5): nothing originated in the preceding year but 1 purchased: more than 50 percent
#ASSERT `exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 0 2 50   -- (k)(5): 1 of 2 originated is exactly 50 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1 0 1.99 50))   -- (k)(5): 1 of 1.99 is just over 50 percent
-- (l): an intraday extension of credit to an affiliate, if the bank (i) has and maintains policies and procedures reasonably designed to manage the credit exposure, including (A) monitoring and controlling the exposure to each affiliate and all affiliates in the aggregate
-- and (B) ensuring market terms; (ii) has no reason to believe the affiliate will have difficulty repaying; and (iii) ceases to treat it as intraday at the end of the bank's business day in the United States.
-- (l)(2): an intraday extension of credit is one the bank expects to be repaid, sold, or terminated, or to qualify for a complete exemption, by the end of its business day in the United States.
#ASSERT `exempt as an intraday extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE   -- (l): every condition satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an intraday extension of credit` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE))   -- (l): only expectedToEndByTheEndOfTheBusinessDay is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an intraday extension of credit` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))   -- (l): only policiesAndProceduresMonitorExposure is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an intraday extension of credit` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE))   -- (l): only policiesAndProceduresEnsureMarketTerms is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an intraday extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))   -- (l): only noReasonToBelieveRepaymentWillBeDifficult is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as an intraday extension of credit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))   -- (l): only ceasesToTreatItAsIntradayAtTheEndOfTheDay is not satisfied
-- (m): purchasing a security from a securities affiliate if (1) the bank or the securities affiliate acts exclusively as a riskless principal, and (2) the security is not issued, underwritten or sold as principal (other than riskless principal) by any affiliate.
#ASSERT `exempt as a riskless principal purchase` TRUE TRUE TRUE   -- (m): every condition satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a riskless principal purchase` FALSE TRUE TRUE))   -- (m): only fromASecuritiesAffiliate is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a riskless principal purchase` TRUE FALSE TRUE))   -- (m): only actingExclusivelyAsARisklessPrincipal is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a riskless principal purchase` TRUE TRUE FALSE))   -- (m): only notIssuedUnderwrittenOrSoldAsPrincipalByAnAffiliate is not satisfied
-- (n): from September 15, 2008, until October 30, 2009 (unless the Board extends it), a securities financing transaction with an affiliate, if (i) to (v).  The period flag is an input.
#ASSERT `exempt as a securities financing transaction` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE   -- (n): every condition satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a securities financing transaction` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE))   -- (n): only periodIsRunning is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a securities financing transaction` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE))   -- (n): only isASecuritiesFinancingTransaction is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a securities financing transaction` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE))   -- (n): only ofATypeFinancedInTheTriPartyMarketInThatWeek is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a securities financing transaction` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))   -- (n): only markedToMarketDailyAndAtLeastAsOverCollateralized is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a securities financing transaction` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE))   -- (n): only aggregateRiskProfileNoGreater is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a securities financing transaction` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))   -- (n): only topTierHoldingCompanyGuarantees is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a securities financing transaction` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))   -- (n): only notInformedByTheBoardItMayNotUseIt is not satisfied
-- (o): purchases of asset-backed commercial paper from an affiliated SEC-registered open-end investment company that holds itself out as a money market mutual fund, if the bank (1) buys on or after September 19, 2008, (2) pledges it to a Federal Reserve Bank for AMLF financing, and (3) has not been told by the Board that it may not use the exemption.
#ASSERT `exempt as a purchase of asset-backed commercial paper` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE   -- (o): every condition satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of asset-backed commercial paper` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))   -- (o): only fromAnAffiliatedMoneyMarketFund is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of asset-backed commercial paper` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE))   -- (o): only boughtOnOrAfterSeptember19Of2008 is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of asset-backed commercial paper` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))   -- (o): only pledgedToAFederalReserveBankForAmlfFinancing is not satisfied
#ASSERT (NOT (`exempt as a purchase of asset-backed commercial paper` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))   -- (o): only notInformedByTheBoardItMayNotUseIt is not satisfied

§ `The effects of an exemption: which requirements remain`

-- 223.41: not subject to 223.11, 223.12 or 223.14; subject to 223.13 and 223.15.
-- 223.42: not subject to 223.11, 223.12, 223.14 or 223.15; subject to 223.13.
-- 223.16(c): not subject to 223.11, 223.12 or 223.14; subject to 223.13 (and subpart F).
-- No exemption: every requirement applies.
-- The single case on which these words say nothing, 223.15 for a 223.16(c) transaction, is in `Contested readings` (R6).
#ASSERT `requirement still applies` `No exemption` `The single-affiliate limit of 223.11`   -- no exemption: 223.11 still applies
#ASSERT `requirement still applies` `No exemption` `The all-affiliates limit of 223.12`   -- no exemption: 223.12 still applies
#ASSERT `requirement still applies` `No exemption` `The safety and soundness requirement of 223.13`   -- no exemption: 223.13 still applies
#ASSERT `requirement still applies` `No exemption` `The collateral requirements of 223.14`   -- no exemption: 223.14 still applies
#ASSERT `requirement still applies` `No exemption` `The low-quality asset prohibition of 223.15`   -- no exemption: 223.15 still applies
#ASSERT (NOT (`requirement still applies` `An exemption under 223.41` `The single-affiliate limit of 223.11`))   -- an exemption under 223.41: 223.11 does not apply
#ASSERT (NOT (`requirement still applies` `An exemption under 223.41` `The all-affiliates limit of 223.12`))   -- an exemption under 223.41: 223.12 does not apply
#ASSERT `requirement still applies` `An exemption under 223.41` `The safety and soundness requirement of 223.13`   -- an exemption under 223.41: 223.13 still applies
#ASSERT (NOT (`requirement still applies` `An exemption under 223.41` `The collateral requirements of 223.14`))   -- an exemption under 223.41: 223.14 does not apply
#ASSERT `requirement still applies` `An exemption under 223.41` `The low-quality asset prohibition of 223.15`   -- an exemption under 223.41: 223.15 still applies
#ASSERT (NOT (`requirement still applies` `An exemption under 223.42` `The single-affiliate limit of 223.11`))   -- an exemption under 223.42: 223.11 does not apply
#ASSERT (NOT (`requirement still applies` `An exemption under 223.42` `The all-affiliates limit of 223.12`))   -- an exemption under 223.42: 223.12 does not apply
#ASSERT `requirement still applies` `An exemption under 223.42` `The safety and soundness requirement of 223.13`   -- an exemption under 223.42: 223.13 still applies
#ASSERT (NOT (`requirement still applies` `An exemption under 223.42` `The collateral requirements of 223.14`))   -- an exemption under 223.42: 223.14 does not apply
#ASSERT (NOT (`requirement still applies` `An exemption under 223.42` `The low-quality asset prohibition of 223.15`))   -- an exemption under 223.42: 223.15 does not apply
#ASSERT (NOT (`requirement still applies` `An exemption under 223.16(c)` `The single-affiliate limit of 223.11`))   -- an exemption under 223.16(c): 223.11 does not apply
#ASSERT (NOT (`requirement still applies` `An exemption under 223.16(c)` `The all-affiliates limit of 223.12`))   -- an exemption under 223.16(c): 223.12 does not apply
#ASSERT `requirement still applies` `An exemption under 223.16(c)` `The safety and soundness requirement of 223.13`   -- an exemption under 223.16(c): 223.13 still applies
#ASSERT (NOT (`requirement still applies` `An exemption under 223.16(c)` `The collateral requirements of 223.14`))   -- an exemption under 223.16(c): 223.14 does not apply

§ `The assessment of a proposed transaction`

-- End-to-end scenarios.  The bank's capital stock and surplus is 1000 unless stated, so the single-affiliate limit is 100 and the all-affiliates limit is 200.
-- assessment of a proposed transaction structure readings transaction situation collateral exceptions asset-facts
-- Situation OF capital stock and surplus; outstanding covered transactions with this affiliate; outstanding with all affiliates; on safe and sound terms; exemption claimed; value exempt.
-- Each scenario asserts only the fields the words of 223.3(h), 223.11 to 223.15, 223.41 and 223.42 determine.
-- `value exempt` is 0 unless an exemption is claimed; for a transaction exempt altogether it is the transaction's full value.
-- --- The limits ---
-- Scenario 01: a loan of exactly 10 percent of capital stock and surplus to a parent, fully secured by Treasuries
`scenario 01` MEANS `assessment of a proposed transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE) (Situation OF 1000, 0, 0, TRUE, `No exemption`, 0) (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 100)) `no exceptions` (`Asset purchase facts` OF `a sound asset`, FALSE, FALSE, `no renewal`, pp)
#ASSERT `scenario 01`'s `is a covered transaction`   -- scenario 01, is a covered transaction
#ASSERT `scenario 01`'s `amount that counts toward the limits` EQUALS 100   -- scenario 01, amount that counts toward the limits
#ASSERT (NOT (`scenario 01`'s `breaches the single-affiliate limit`))   -- scenario 01, breaches the single-affiliate limit
