`scenario 64` MEANS `assessment of a proposed transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE) (Situation OF 1000, 500, 500, TRUE, `No exemption`, 0) (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 100)) `no exceptions` (`Asset purchase facts` OF `a sound asset`, FALSE, FALSE, `no renewal`, pp)
#ASSERT `scenario 64`'s `is a covered transaction`   -- scenario 64, is a covered transaction
#ASSERT `scenario 64`'s `breaches the single-affiliate limit`   -- scenario 64, breaches the single-affiliate limit
#ASSERT `scenario 64`'s `breaches the all-affiliates limit`   -- scenario 64, breaches the all-affiliates limit
#ASSERT (NOT (`scenario 64`'s `may be entered into`))   -- scenario 64, may be entered into


§ `Contested readings`

-- Each assertion below depends on a reading of the words that is genuinely open.  Each names its R-number in independent-readings-b.md,
-- which gives the words that fork, the reading the assertion takes, and what the other reading would give.
-- R1: which company does 223.3(h) test for affiliation?  Reading A (taken): the affiliate concerned (the issuer, or the company on whose behalf a guarantee is given), with the counterparty free to be a nonaffiliate.
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAccept, "Stranger Corp", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE)   -- R1 reading A: (h)(4): the borrower is a nonaffiliate, the collateral is a security issued by the affiliate
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kGuarantee, "Stranger Corp", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE)   -- R1 reading A: (h)(5): the guarantee runs to a nonaffiliate beneficiary on behalf of the affiliate
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kNetting, "Stranger Corp", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE)   -- R1 reading A: (h)(5): a cross-affiliate netting arrangement is among the bank, affiliates and nonaffiliates
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAccept, "Acme Holdings", "Stranger Corp", 100, FALSE)))   -- R1 reading A: (h)(4) concerns a security issued by the AFFILIATE: a nonaffiliate's security taken as collateral for a loan to a parent is not within (h)(4) (reading B, testing the counterparty, would say covered)
-- Scenario 65: R1 reading A: acceptance of a parent's securities as collateral for a 40 loan to a nonaffiliate: 223.3(h)(4) covers it
`scenario 65` MEANS `assessment of a proposed transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAccept, "Stranger Corp", "Acme Holdings", 40, FALSE) (Situation OF 1000, 0, 0, TRUE, `No exemption`, 0) EMPTY `no exceptions` (`Asset purchase facts` OF `a sound asset`, FALSE, FALSE, `no renewal`, pp)
#ASSERT `scenario 65`'s `is a covered transaction`   -- scenario 65, is a covered transaction
#ASSERT `scenario 65`'s `amount that counts toward the limits` EQUALS 40   -- scenario 65, amount that counts toward the limits
#ASSERT (NOT (`scenario 65`'s `breaches the single-affiliate limit`))   -- scenario 65, breaches the single-affiliate limit
#ASSERT (NOT (`scenario 65`'s `breaches the all-affiliates limit`))   -- scenario 65, breaches the all-affiliates limit
#ASSERT `scenario 65`'s `may be entered into`   -- scenario 65, may be entered into

-- R2: 223.15(b)(3) 'does not exceed its proportional share ... by more than 5 percent': percentage points (A) or five percent more (B).  The interface has one constructor for each.
#ASSERT `share is within the five percent allowance` 25 20 pp   -- R2, five percentage points: 25 is exactly 5 points above 20
#ASSERT `share is within the five percent allowance` 21.01 20 pp   -- R2, five percentage points: 21.01 is within 5 points of 20
#ASSERT `share is within the five percent allowance` 5 0 pp   -- R2, five percentage points: 5 is 5 points above 0
#ASSERT (NOT (`share is within the five percent allowance` 25 20 rel))   -- R2, five percent more: 25 is 25 percent more than 20
#ASSERT (NOT (`share is within the five percent allowance` 21.01 20 rel))   -- R2, five percent more: 21.01 exceeds 20 x 1.05 = 21
#ASSERT (NOT (`share is within the five percent allowance` 5 0 rel))   -- R2, five percent more: 5 exceeds 0 x 1.05 = 0
#ASSERT `the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 25, 20, FALSE, 20) pp   -- R2, five percentage points: the renewal exception holds at share 25 against 20
#ASSERT (NOT (`the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 25, 20, FALSE, 20) rel))   -- R2, five percent more: the same renewal fails (b)(3)
#ASSERT `the renewal exception applies` (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 25, 20, TRUE, 20) rel   -- R2, five percent more: with the agency's prior written approval it holds
#ASSERT (NOT (`purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 25, 20, FALSE, 20) pp))   -- R2, five percentage points: the renewal exception lifts the prohibition at share 25 against 20
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE (`Participation renewal` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 25, 20, FALSE, 20) rel   -- R2, five percent more: the same facts are a prohibited purchase
-- R3: 223.14(d)(2) 'deduct ... the lesser of' the senior amounts: if the deduction exceeds the market value, does the effective value stop at 0 (A, taken) or go negative (B)?  Tested through the amount secured, where B would reduce the other collateral.
#ASSERT `amount of the transaction secured by collateral` (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 100), (`encumbered collateral` cUS 100 500 500)) EQUALS 100   -- R3 reading A: the over-encumbered collateral adds 0, it does not subtract 400 from the clean 100
-- R4: 223.14(d)(1) 'must maintain a security interest ... that is perfected and enforceable': where does an unperfected interest bite?  Reading A (taken): not in 223.14(c) eligibility, but in effective value (0).  B: ineligible, effective value ignores perfection.  C: both.
#ASSERT `is eligible collateral` (`unperfected collateral` cUS 100)   -- R4 reading A: 223.14(c) lists no perfection condition, so the kind is eligible
#ASSERT `effective value of collateral` (`unperfected collateral` cUS 100) EQUALS 0   -- R4 reading A: an interest that is not perfected and enforceable is worth nothing (the stub answers 0 too)
-- R5: 223.42(c) 'to the extent that the transaction is and remains secured by' cash or government securities: is the exempt part the collateral's market value (B), or its value after a senior lien (A, taken)?
#ASSERT `exempt part of a credit transaction secured by cash or government securities` 100 (LIST (`encumbered collateral` cUS 100 40 40)) EQUALS 60   -- R5 reading A: Treasuries of 100 behind a senior 40 lien secure 60 of the loan
-- R6: 223.16(c) lists 223.11, 223.12 and 223.14 as the requirements the transactions are not subject to, and keeps 223.13 and subpart F; it says nothing of 223.15.  Reading A (taken): only the three named are lifted, so 223.15 still applies.  B: only 223.13 and subpart F remain.
#ASSERT `requirement still applies` `An exemption under 223.16(c)` `The low-quality asset prohibition of 223.15`   -- R6 reading A
-- R7: when an exemption covers only part of a transaction (223.42(c)), do the limits apply to the remainder (A, taken), or does the claim switch the limits off for the whole transaction (B)?
-- Scenario 66: R7 reading A, the 223.42(c) example: a loan of 100 to a parent secured by Treasuries of 50 and real estate of 75, exempt to the extent of 50, capital stock and surplus 500: the 50 that is left is exactly 10 percent
`scenario 66` MEANS `assessment of a proposed transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE) (Situation OF 500, 0, 0, TRUE, `An exemption under 223.42`, 50) (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 50), (`clean collateral` cProp 75)) `no exceptions` (`Asset purchase facts` OF `a sound asset`, FALSE, FALSE, `no renewal`, pp)
#ASSERT `scenario 66`'s `is a covered transaction`   -- scenario 66, is a covered transaction
#ASSERT `scenario 66`'s `amount that counts toward the limits` EQUALS 50   -- scenario 66, amount that counts toward the limits
#ASSERT (NOT (`scenario 66`'s `breaches the single-affiliate limit`))   -- scenario 66, breaches the single-affiliate limit
#ASSERT (NOT (`scenario 66`'s `breaches the all-affiliates limit`))   -- scenario 66, breaches the all-affiliates limit
#ASSERT `scenario 66`'s `may be entered into`   -- scenario 66, may be entered into

-- Scenario 67: R7 reading A: the same loan with capital stock and surplus 499: the 50 that is left is a cent over 10 percent of 499 (49.9)
`scenario 67` MEANS `assessment of a proposed transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 100, FALSE) (Situation OF 499, 0, 0, TRUE, `An exemption under 223.42`, 50) (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 50), (`clean collateral` cProp 75)) `no exceptions` (`Asset purchase facts` OF `a sound asset`, FALSE, FALSE, `no renewal`, pp)
#ASSERT `scenario 67`'s `is a covered transaction`   -- scenario 67, is a covered transaction
#ASSERT `scenario 67`'s `amount that counts toward the limits` EQUALS 50   -- scenario 67, amount that counts toward the limits
#ASSERT `scenario 67`'s `breaches the single-affiliate limit`   -- scenario 67, breaches the single-affiliate limit
#ASSERT (NOT (`scenario 67`'s `may be entered into`))   -- scenario 67, may be entered into

-- R8: 'amount that counts toward the limits': the transaction's own counted amount, value less value exempt (A, taken), or the aggregate with what is outstanding (B)?  The scenarios above with nothing outstanding give the same answer on both.
-- Scenario 68: R8 reading A: a loan of 60 to a parent with 40 outstanding to it: the amount that counts is 60 (B would say 100)
`scenario 68` MEANS `assessment of a proposed transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Holdings", "Acme Holdings", 60, FALSE) (Situation OF 1000, 40, 40, TRUE, `No exemption`, 0) (LIST (`clean collateral` cUS 60)) `no exceptions` (`Asset purchase facts` OF `a sound asset`, FALSE, FALSE, `no renewal`, pp)
#ASSERT `scenario 68`'s `is a covered transaction`   -- scenario 68, is a covered transaction
#ASSERT `scenario 68`'s `amount that counts toward the limits` EQUALS 60   -- scenario 68, amount that counts toward the limits
#ASSERT (NOT (`scenario 68`'s `breaches the single-affiliate limit`))   -- scenario 68, breaches the single-affiliate limit
#ASSERT `scenario 68`'s `may be entered into`   -- scenario 68, may be entered into

-- R9: 223.24(b) 'the total value of the extension of credit less the fair market value of the nonaffiliate collateral' when that is negative: does the value stop at 0 (A, taken)?  B lets it go negative, giving the lesser of -50 and 50.
#ASSERT `value of credit secured partly by affiliate securities` 100 150 50 TRUE EQUALS 0   -- R9 reading A: nonaffiliate collateral (150) exceeds the credit (100): nothing is left to value (the stub answers 0 too)
-- R10: 223.14(c)(4) makes an intangible asset eligible when the Board specifically approves it, and 223.14(b)(1) lists no percentage for it.  Reading A (taken): it is 'other real or personal property', 130 percent (iv).  B: the words give no percentage.
#ASSERT `percent the collateral must stand at` cIntang EQUALS 130   -- R10 reading A: an intangible asset is personal property: 130 percent under (b)(1)(iv)
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`board approved collateral` cIntang 1000))   -- R10: 1000 of Board-approved intangible assets covers a loan of 100 at any percentage up to 130 (division by a zero percent would be an error)
#ASSERT `collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`board approved collateral` cIntang 130))   -- R10 reading A: exactly 130 percent of a loan of 100
#ASSERT (NOT (`collateral requirement is met` kCredit 100 `no exceptions` (LIST (`board approved collateral` cIntang 129.99))))   -- R10 reading A: a cent under 130 percent of a loan of 100
-- R11: not a fork in slice B's own words: slice A carries a switch for whether the member bank is its own affiliate (223.2(a)(2) with 223.3(f)).  These assertions only check that the `Readings` handed to slice B reach the affiliate lookup.
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Bank", "Acme Bank", 100, FALSE)))   -- R11, the member bank is not its own affiliate: a loan to the bank itself is not a covered transaction
#ASSERT `is a covered transaction` `the structure` `the literal readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Bank", "Acme Bank", 100, FALSE)   -- R11, the member bank is its own affiliate on the literal words: the same loan is a covered transaction
#ASSERT `would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the literal readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Bank", "Acme Bank", 100.01, FALSE) 0 1000   -- R11, literal words: the bank as its own affiliate is within 223.11: 100.01 is a cent over 10 percent
#ASSERT (NOT (`would breach the single-affiliate limit` `the structure` `the readings` (Transaction OF kCredit, "Acme Bank", "Acme Bank", 100.01, FALSE) 0 1000))   -- R11, not its own affiliate: the same transaction is not a covered transaction, so no breach
#ASSERT `purchase of a low-quality asset is prohibited` `the structure` `the literal readings` (Transaction OF kAsset, "Acme Bank", "Acme Bank", 50, FALSE) (`Asset condition` OF FALSE, TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE `no renewal` pp   -- R11, literal words: a nonaccrual asset bought from the bank itself, as its own affiliate

